Object.assign(window.IND_FEED_BODY, {"ss-fk.karam-brothers-2":{"src":"story:fk.karam-brothers:scenes:2:text","title":"The Branch the Brothers Brought Home · 3 of 9","body":"Then came a busy year. Trade was good, the brothers were rich and rushing, and when the festival came round, they had no time. The drums played in other courtyards. In theirs, nothing — and in some tellings the sacred branch was not just forgotten but knocked aside in the hurry, which is worse.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-karam-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.karam-brothers|s2","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from The Branch the Brothers Brought Home","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"ss-fk.karam-brothers-3":{"src":"story:fk.karam-brothers:scenes:3:text","title":"The Branch the Brothers Brought Home · 4 of 9","body":"And the luck left. Quietly, completely, the way a guest leaves a house where no one greets her. The rice sickened, the cattle strayed, the granary emptied, and within the year the famous brothers were poor men staring at each other across a bare table.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-karam-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.karam-brothers|s3","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from The Branch the Brothers Brought Home","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"ss-fk.karam-brothers-5":{"src":"story:fk.karam-brothers:scenes:5:text","title":"The Branch the Brothers Brought Home · 6 of 9","body":"So the brothers walked. The tellings send them far — across rivers, through forests, asking everyone they met where the spirit of the karam might be found. And the search itself began to change them: two men who had had no time for anything now had time for everything, and helped whoever they met on the road, because they finally knew how it felt to need help.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-karam-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.karam-brothers|s5","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from The Branch the Brothers Brought Home","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"ss-fk.karam-brothers-6":{"src":"story:fk.karam-brothers:scenes:6:text","title":"The Branch the Brothers Brought Home · 7 of 9","body":"At last, by the water, they found the karam — and they asked its forgiveness, plainly, the way you ask when you mean it. And they cut one branch with honour, and carried it home high, singing the songs their mother had taught them, every verse, the whole way back.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-karam-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.karam-brothers|s6","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from The Branch the Brothers Brought Home","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"ss-fk.karam-brothers-7":{"src":"story:fk.karam-brothers:scenes:7:text","title":"The Branch the Brothers Brought Home · 8 of 9","body":"They planted the branch in their courtyard, and the household danced around it all night — and the luck came home the way the branch had: carried, honoured, sung to. The fields recovered. The brothers did not forget again. Nobody who has walked that far for a branch forgets again.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-karam-brothers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.karam-brothers|s7","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from The Branch the Brothers Brought Home","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"ss-fk.bamboo-bonga-1":{"src":"story:fk.bamboo-bonga:scenes:1:text","title":"The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo · 2 of 9","body":"Every winter, when the forest grew lean, the elephant came up the hill to the great bamboo grove and ate. The grove always had enough: green canes at the edges, sweet shoots in the softer ground. He ate, rumbled his thanks in the general direction of nothing, and ambled off. It had worked this way his whole life.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bamboo-bonga.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bamboo-bonga|s1","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"ss-fk.bamboo-bonga-2":{"src":"story:fk.bamboo-bonga:scenes:2:text","title":"The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo · 3 of 9","body":"But this winter was hungrier than most, and standing in the middle of all that bamboo, the elephant had a big grey thought: why nibble at the edges? He could push the whole grove flat in an afternoon and feast for a week — the hearts of the clumps, the young shoots, everything, all at once.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bamboo-bonga.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bamboo-bonga|s2","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"ss-fk.bamboo-bonga-3":{"src":"story:fk.bamboo-bonga:scenes:3:text","title":"The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo · 4 of 9","body":"He had wrapped his trunk around the first great clump when the grove spoke. Not loudly. Bongas rarely need to be loud. It was a voice like wind through canes, coming from everywhere and nowhere: \"Winter guest. Before you pull — a question.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bamboo-bonga.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bamboo-bonga|s3","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"ss-fk.bamboo-bonga-5":{"src":"story:fk.bamboo-bonga:scenes:5:text","title":"The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo · 6 of 9","body":"\"...This grove,\" he said at last, very quietly. \"If there is one.\" He let go of the clump. It swayed back upright, and the whole grove rustled — with relief, or laughter; with bamboo it is hard to tell the difference.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bamboo-bonga.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bamboo-bonga|s5","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"ss-fk.bamboo-bonga-6":{"src":"story:fk.bamboo-bonga:scenes:6:text","title":"The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo · 7 of 9","body":"\"Then here is the grove's law, guest,\" said the bonga. \"Take from the edges, where I grow back. Leave the hearts, where I live. Eat your fill and leave me standing — and I will feed you, and your calves, and their calves, every winter until elephants forget the way here. That is a better bargain than one loud afternoon.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bamboo-bonga.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bamboo-bonga|s6","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"ss-fk.bamboo-bonga-7":{"src":"story:fk.bamboo-bonga:scenes:7:text","title":"The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo · 8 of 9","body":"The elephant ate from the edges — a very large amount, it must be said; the law says fill, and he filled. Then he touched the oldest cane gently with his trunk, the way you touch an elder's feet, and went back down the hill. And the next winter the grove was there. And the next. And the next.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bamboo-bonga.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bamboo-bonga|s7","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from The Elephant and the Keeper of the Bamboo","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"ss-fk.sarhul-flowers-1":{"src":"story:fk.sarhul-flowers:scenes:1:text","title":"When the Sal Trees Bloom · 2 of 8","body":"It is kept, in their own ways, by many peoples of the plateau — the Oraon, the Munda, the Ho and others keep Sarhul, and the Santhals keep their own flower festival, Baha, in the same blossoming season. Different songs, different steps, one shared idea: the year begins when the trees say so.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sarhul-flowers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sarhul-flowers|s1","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from When the Sal Trees Bloom","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"ss-fk.sarhul-flowers-2":{"src":"story:fk.sarhul-flowers:scenes:2:text","title":"When the Sal Trees Bloom · 3 of 8","body":"The festival goes to the sacred grove first. The village priest — the pahan — keeps the rites there on behalf of everyone, with offerings and prayers for good rains and a good year; in many villages the pahan reads the signs from vessels of water, and the village listens to what the water promises about the monsoon.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sarhul-flowers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sarhul-flowers|s2","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from When the Sal Trees Bloom","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"ss-fk.sarhul-flowers-3":{"src":"story:fk.sarhul-flowers:scenes:3:text","title":"When the Sal Trees Bloom · 4 of 8","body":"Then the grove's blessing comes home. Sal blossoms are carried from the grove and set with honour on doorways and in houses — the priest and elders bringing flowers to every family, so that every roof in the village wears a piece of the forest's spring. Drums begin. Lines of dancers form. It goes on into the night, and nobody is in a hurry for it to stop.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sarhul-flowers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sarhul-flowers|s3","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from When the Sal Trees Bloom","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"ss-fk.sarhul-flowers-5":{"src":"story:fk.sarhul-flowers:scenes:5:text","title":"When the Sal Trees Bloom · 6 of 8","body":"In Ranchi, Sarhul has grown into one of the great sights of the city: processions from every neighbourhood, rivers of dancers and drummers in white saris bordered with red, sal blossoms everywhere, the whole capital walking and singing. Schools close. The plateau celebrates itself.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sarhul-flowers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sarhul-flowers|s5","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from When the Sal Trees Bloom","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"ss-fk.sarhul-flowers-6":{"src":"story:fk.sarhul-flowers:scenes:6:text","title":"When the Sal Trees Bloom · 7 of 8","body":"And through it all stand the trees that started it — the sal, the tree of the plateau, giver of leaf-plates and resin and shade and timber and this one week of perfume. The festival is, at its heart, a whole people turning to a forest and saying, formally and with drums: we noticed. Thank you. Again this year.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-sarhul-flowers.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.sarhul-flowers|s6","cta":"Read from here","why":"A moment from When the Sal Trees Bloom","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["Read","4 min"]]},"en-ramayana-21-1":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|21","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":21},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:20:cards:1:text","title":"The Ramayana · The Long Nights","body":"It was not glorious either. The vanaras went up ladders made of each other and came down again. The gates held. It rained. Rama walked the lines at night and learned the names of people who were not there the next night, and the tellings that are honest do not skip that part.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 21","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","21 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-21-2":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|21","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":21},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:20:cards:2:text","title":"The Ramayana · The Long Nights","body":"Indrajit was the worst of it. Ravana's eldest, and he fought from inside a cloud where nobody could see him, and on the third night he brought both brothers down at once with arrows that turned into serpents and wound them up on the ground where they lay.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 21","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","21 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-21-3":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|21","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":21},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:20:cards:3:text","title":"The Ramayana · The Long Nights","body":"The whole army sat down around them in the dark. That was the low point. And then something came over the sea at dawn like a wind with wings — Garuda, the great eagle, who is the enemy of every serpent there is — and every snake on that field simply let go and left.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 21","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","21 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-21-4":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|21","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":21},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:20:cards:4:text","title":"The Ramayana · The Long Nights","body":"Kumbhakarna came out on the fifth day, enormous and slow and sad, and he had said what he had to say to his brother already and had nothing left to say to anybody. He did a great deal of damage. When he fell, the ground jumped, and Ravana in his tower put his hands over his face and stayed like that for a long time.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 21","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","21 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-21-5":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|21","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":21},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:20:cards:5:text","title":"The Ramayana · The Long Nights","body":"On the seventh night Indrajit came back out of his cloud and hit Lakshmana with something nobody could stop. He went down and did not get up. Rama got to him first and could not get an answer out of him, and sat down on the ground in the middle of a battlefield holding his brother and stopped being any use to anybody at all.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 21","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","21 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-21-7":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|21","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":21},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:20:cards:7:text","title":"The Ramayana · The Long Nights","body":"Every head on that field turned to the same person. Hanuman was already standing up.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 21","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","21 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-21-8":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|21","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":21},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:20:cards:8:text","title":"The Ramayana · The Long Nights","body":"He went north over the whole subcontinent in the dark — over the bridge, over the forest, over the rivers, over the plains where his story would be told for the next three thousand years — and came down on a mountain in the snow, and looked at it.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 21","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","21 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-21-9":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|21","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":21},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:20:cards:9:text","title":"The Ramayana · The Long Nights","body":"And the mountain was covered, absolutely covered, in small glowing plants, thousands of them, and every one of them looked exactly the same. He stood in the snow with the sky already going grey in the east, and said out loud, \"I do not know which one it is.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 21","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","21 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-21-10":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|21","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":21},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:20:cards:10:text","title":"The Ramayana · The Long Nights","body":"So he did not choose. He got his arms round the mountain, and pulled it out of the Himalaya, and carried the entire thing back south on one hand, and the story is told all over India of the night people looked up and saw a mountain going over their village.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 21","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","21 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-22-1":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|22","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":22},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:21:cards:1:text","title":"The Ramayana · Ravana","body":"\"My brother is out there in their army,\" said Ravana. \"My son is dead. Kumbhakarna is dead. What do I say to them at the end of a day like that? That I was wrong all along and I only stopped when it got expensive?\" \"Yes,\" said Mandodari. \"You say that. That is exactly what you say. It would be the bravest thing you ever did.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 22","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","22 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-22-2":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|22","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":22},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:21:cards:2:text","title":"The Ramayana · Ravana","body":"He stood in the doorway of his own hall for a while. Then he said, \"I cannot,\" and went out to the chariot, and that is the whole tragedy of Ravana in three words, and everything else is just how long it took.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 22","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","22 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-22-3":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|22","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":22},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:21:cards:3:text","title":"The Ramayana · Ravana","body":"He came out onto the field and it was quite a sight. He was magnificent. Nobody on that field had ever seen anything like him, and there is not a version of this story anywhere that pretends otherwise.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 22","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","22 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-22-4":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|22","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":22},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:21:cards:4:text","title":"The Ramayana · Ravana","body":"Rama was on foot. So Indra sent down a chariot for him, with a driver called Matali, and Rama said thank you to the driver and asked his name, which Matali mentioned to people for the rest of his life.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 22","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","22 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-22-5":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|22","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":22},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:21:cards:5:text","title":"The Ramayana · Ravana","body":"They fought all day and neither of them could finish it, and the two armies stopped fighting each other and simply stood and watched, which is a thing that has never happened in any other battle in any other story.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 22","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","22 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-22-7":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|22","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":22},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:21:cards:7:text","title":"The Ramayana · Ravana","body":"Lanka went absolutely silent. And then Mandodari came out of the gate and walked across that field alone to where he had fallen, and knelt down, and said, \"You were the cleverest man in the world, and you would not be told. Not by me, not by your brother, not by your own son. All this. For one thing you could have undone in a morning.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 22","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","22 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-22-8":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|22","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":22},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:21:cards:8:text","title":"The Ramayana · Ravana","body":"Vibhishana would not do the funeral rites at first. He said the man had thrown him out of his own house. Rama said: \"He is not your enemy any more. That ended this evening. He is your brother, and he was a great king, and you will do it properly, and I will stand there while you do.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 22","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","22 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-22-9":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|22","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":22},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:21:cards:9:text","title":"The Ramayana · Ravana","body":"And in some tellings — this is not in Valmiki, but it is told in a good many homes and it is loved — Rama sends Lakshmana across the field to sit at Ravana's head and ask him for whatever he has left to teach, because there was more learning in that man than anyone alive, and it would be a waste to let it go into the ground.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 22","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","22 of 24"]]},"en-ramayana-22-10":{"route":"#/epic/ramayana|22","act":{"a":"episode","id":"ramayana","n":22},"src":"epic:ramayana:episodes:21:cards:10:text","title":"The Ramayana · Ravana","body":"The war was over. It had taken most of a month. The vanaras did not cheer for very long, because they were counting who was left, and a great many of them were not.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Ramayana, night 22","facts":[["Epic","The Ramayana"],["Night","22 of 24"]]},"en-mahabharata-14-1":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|14","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":14},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:13:cards:1:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Draupadi's Question","body":"\"Go and ask my husband this. When he staked me — had he already lost himself? Because if he had, then he was not his own man. And a man who does not own himself cannot stake anybody else. So ask the hall: whose was I, at that moment?\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 14","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","14 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-14-2":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|14","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":14},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:13:cards:2:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Draupadi's Question","body":"The messenger carried it back and said it out loud, and the hall had no answer. Yudhishthira sat and looked at the floor and did not speak. He never answers it. Not that day, not in the forest, not in thirteen years.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 14","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","14 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-14-3":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|14","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":14},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:13:cards:3:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Draupadi's Question","body":"So Duryodhana sent his brother Duhshasana to bring her by force, and he did, and she was dragged into the hall in front of her husbands and her elders and everybody in the kingdom who mattered.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 14","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","14 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-14-4":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|14","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":14},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:13:cards:4:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Draupadi's Question","body":"What happened next in that hall is the reason people still say the name of this family with their jaw set. We are not going to describe it. In many tellings something stops it; the manuscripts do not all tell it the same way. What every version agrees on is what the room did, which is nothing.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 14","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","14 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-14-5":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|14","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":14},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:13:cards:5:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Draupadi's Question","body":"She asked her question again, standing up, to the whole hall. And she asked it of the one man there whose whole life was made of keeping his word.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 14","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","14 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-14-6":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|14","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":14},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:13:cards:6:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Draupadi's Question","body":"\"The law about who owns what is subtle,\" said Bhishma slowly, \"and I cannot see the bottom of it. I do not know the answer to your question.\" An old man who had never once been unsure of anything, saying that, in that room.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 14","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","14 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-14-8":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|14","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":14},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:13:cards:8:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Draupadi's Question","body":"And it was Karna who shouted him down. Karna, who had been turned away at a gate himself, said the cruellest thing said in that hall all day, and he said it to her. The most sympathetic person in this poem is on the wrong side of this room, doing the worst thing he ever does.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 14","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","14 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-14-9":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|14","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":14},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:13:cards:9:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Draupadi's Question","body":"Bhima made an oath about Duhshasana's hands so violent that the court flinched. Draupadi untied her hair and said it would stay untied until she had a reason to bind it up again, and everybody there understood exactly what she meant.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 14","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","14 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-14-10":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|14","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":14},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:13:cards:10:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Draupadi's Question","body":"And then jackals started calling in the courtyard in broad daylight, and the old blind king, who had let all of it happen because it was his son doing it, got frightened.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 14","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","14 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-14-11":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|14","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":14},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:13:cards:11:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Draupadi's Question","body":"\"Ask me for anything,\" said Dhritarashtra. She asked for her husbands' freedom. \"Ask again.\" She asked for their weapons and their chariots back. \"Ask a third time.\" And she said no.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 14","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","14 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-14-12":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|14","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":14},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:13:cards:12:text","title":"The Mahabharata · Draupadi's Question","body":"\"I have asked twice, and a person may ask twice,\" she said. \"Whatever else we need, my husbands can fetch for themselves.\" She got it. She walked out of that hall with everything she had come to get, and the question still lying on the floor.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 14","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","14 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-15-1":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|15","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":15},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:14:cards:1:text","title":"The Mahabharata · One More Throw","body":"Then Duryodhana went to his father, with Shakuni behind him, and said what people say when they are winning and have been made to stop: \"You gave it all back. In one afternoon you gave away everything I won. Do you know what they will do with it?\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 15","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","15 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-15-2":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|15","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":15},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:14:cards:2:text","title":"The Mahabharata · One More Throw","body":"Gandhari came and stood in that room, with the cloth over her eyes, and said the only completely sensible sentence anybody says in the entire Sabha Parva.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 15","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","15 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-15-3":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|15","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":15},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:14:cards:3:text","title":"The Mahabharata · One More Throw","body":"\"Send him away,\" she said. \"Today. He is my son and I have carried him and I am telling you he is going to burn this house down with all of us inside it. You can still do it this morning. You will not be able to do it next year.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 15","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","15 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-15-4":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|15","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":15},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:14:cards:4:text","title":"The Mahabharata · One More Throw","body":"\"I cannot,\" said Dhritarashtra. \"He is my son.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 15","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","15 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-15-5":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|15","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":15},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:14:cards:5:text","title":"The Mahabharata · One More Throw","body":"That is the whole tragedy in six words, and every parent who reads it feels the floor go. He was not a wicked man. He was a man who could never once say no to his child, and the price of that was counted out at the end in bodies.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 15","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","15 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-15-7":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|15","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":15},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:14:cards:7:text","title":"The Mahabharata · One More Throw","body":"The loser would go into the forest for twelve years. And then a thirteenth year, living somewhere in the world in disguise — and if anybody recognised them in that thirteenth year, the whole thing started again from the beginning.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 15","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","15 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-15-8":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|15","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":15},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:14:cards:8:text","title":"The Mahabharata · One More Throw","body":"Yudhishthira sat down and picked the dice up. Again. Knowing exactly who he was playing, exactly how it had gone the day before, and exactly what it had already cost his wife.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 15","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","15 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-15-9":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|15","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":15},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:14:cards:9:text","title":"The Mahabharata · One More Throw","body":"He lost.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 15","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","15 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-15-10":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|15","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":15},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:14:cards:10:text","title":"The Mahabharata · One More Throw","body":"They changed into bark and deerskin in the courtyard and walked out through the city they had grown up in, and the people of Hastinapura came out and lined the road and cried, and nobody in the palace came to the gate.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 15","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","15 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-16-1":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|16","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":16},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:15:cards:1:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Longest Argument in the Forest","body":"The argument is this. Draupadi and Bhima want to go back and take the kingdom now. Yudhishthira gave his word for thirteen years and will not move. And Arjuna, mostly, sits between them and says nothing, which does not help.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 16","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","16 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-16-2":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|16","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":16},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:15:cards:2:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Longest Argument in the Forest","body":"\"You are not even angry,\" Draupadi said to him one night. \"That is the part I cannot forgive. I was dragged into a hall. You sat and looked at the floor. And now we are in a wood eating roots and you are calm.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 16","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","16 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-16-3":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|16","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":16},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:15:cards:3:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Longest Argument in the Forest","body":"\"I am not asking you to be a good man,\" she said. \"You are a good man, everybody knows, it is the only thing anyone ever says about you. I am asking you to be angry for one hour. Just one.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 16","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","16 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-16-4":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|16","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":16},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:15:cards:4:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Longest Argument in the Forest","body":"\"If I am good only when it pays,\" said Yudhishthira, \"then I was never good, I was only lucky. I gave my word for thirteen years. I am not going to spend thirteen years explaining to people why my word does not count.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 16","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","16 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-16-5":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|16","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":16},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:15:cards:5:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Longest Argument in the Forest","body":"\"Thirteen years,\" said Bhima, poking the fire. \"I could do the whole thing in an afternoon. Give me the afternoon.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 16","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","16 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-16-7":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|16","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":16},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:15:cards:7:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Longest Argument in the Forest","body":"One thing did happen. Draupadi wanted a particular flower she had seen come down a stream, and Bhima went off up the mountain to find where it grew, shouting and knocking trees over the way he did.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 16","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","16 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-16-8":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|16","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":16},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:15:cards:8:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Longest Argument in the Forest","body":"An old monkey was lying across the path with its tail stretched right over it, and would not move. \"Step over me,\" it said. \"I am old.\" \"I will not step over you, that is rude. Move it.\" \"Move it yourself, boy. I am tired.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 16","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","16 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-16-9":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|16","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":16},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:15:cards:9:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Longest Argument in the Forest","body":"Bhima bent down to flick the tail aside with one hand, and could not shift it. Then both hands. Then everything he had. And the old monkey watched him with great interest and said, \"Yes. It is like that sometimes.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 16","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","16 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-16-10":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|16","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":16},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:15:cards:10:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Longest Argument in the Forest","body":"Bhima stopped and looked at him properly and went down on the path. \"You are Hanuman.\" \"And you are my brother,\" said Hanuman. \"Sons of the wind, both of us. Go and get the flower. And when your day comes, look up at your brother's chariot. I will be on the flag.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 16","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","16 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-17-1":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|17","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":17},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:16:cards:1:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Hunter on the Mountain","body":"Then a wild boar came crashing through the scrub straight at him, and he had a bow in his hands before he had finished thinking about it, and he shot.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 17","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","17 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-17-2":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|17","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":17},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:16:cards:2:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Hunter on the Mountain","body":"So did somebody else. Two arrows, one boar, the same instant. And out of the trees came a huge hunter with a bow, in skins, with a woman walking behind him, entirely at home up there where nobody lives.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 17","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","17 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-17-3":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|17","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":17},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:16:cards:3:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Hunter on the Mountain","body":"\"My kill,\" said the hunter cheerfully. \"I saw it first.\" \"You did not,\" said Arjuna, who had been standing on one leg for weeks and was not in a reasonable frame of mind. \"It came at me. It is mine.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 17","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","17 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-17-4":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|17","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":17},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:16:cards:4:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Hunter on the Mountain","body":"They argued about a pig on a mountainside like two boys at a village fair. Then they shot at each other, and then they wrestled, and Arjuna — the finest archer alive, the one who only ever sees the eye — lost.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 17","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","17 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-17-5":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|17","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":17},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:16:cards:5:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Hunter on the Mountain","body":"He lost his arrows, which came back empty. He lost his bow. He lost the fight with his hands. He ended up flat on the stones with nothing left, which had never once happened to him in his life.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 17","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","17 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-17-7":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|17","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":17},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:16:cards:7:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Hunter on the Mountain","body":"And when he looked up, the flowers were sitting on the hunter's head.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 17","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","17 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-17-8":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|17","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":17},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:16:cards:8:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Hunter on the Mountain","body":"He got up very slowly. \"You,\" he said. And Shiva laughed at him, standing there in his skins with the flowers on, and said, \"You fought me for an hour and you were not bad.\"","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 17","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","17 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-17-9":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|17","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":17},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:16:cards:9:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Hunter on the Mountain","body":"\"Nobody comes up here to be told they are wonderful,\" said Shiva. \"You came up to be beaten. Now you have been, so you can be given something.\" And he gave him the weapon that Arjuna would carry all the way to the last day and, in the end, would not use.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 17","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","17 of 33"]]},"en-mahabharata-17-10":{"route":"#/epic/mahabharata|17","act":{"a":"episode","id":"mahabharata","n":17},"src":"epic:mahabharata:episodes:16:cards:10:text","title":"The Mahabharata · The Hunter on the Mountain","body":"Arjuna stayed away five years in all. He learned things, and he was taught to dance and to sing by the musicians of the sky, which sounds like a joke and turns out — exactly one book later — to be the thing that saves all five of them.","art":null,"cta":"Hear this night","why":"The Mahabharata, night 17","facts":[["Epic","The Mahabharata"],["Night","17 of 33"]]},"hp-dv.what-is-an-avatar-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.what-is-an-avatar:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Word That Means Coming Down","text":"\"तुम यह शब्द पहले से ही जानते हो। जब तुम किसी खेल में कोई छोटा सा किरदार बनाते हो और उसे उस दुनिया में भेजते हो, तो तुम उसे अपना अवतार कहते हो। यह शब्द संस्कृत का है, और यह किसी भी खेल से कहीं ज़्यादा पुराना है। अवतार। इसका मतलब है—नीचे उतरना।\"","lang":"hi","body":"You already know the word. When you make a little person in a game and send them into the world, you call it your avatar. That word is Sanskrit, and it is much older than any game. Avatara. It means a coming-down.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-what-is-an-avatar.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.what-is-an-avatar|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.what-is-an-avatar-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.what-is-an-avatar:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Word That Means Coming Down","text":"\"विष्णु की कहानियों में, जब दुनिया का संतुलन बहुत डगमगा जाता है—जब कोई बात इतनी बिगड़ जाती है कि दुनिया का कोई भी इंसान उसे ठीक नहीं कर सकता—तब विष्णु उसे ठीक करने के लिए दुनिया के अंदर उतर आते हैं। ऊपर से सिर्फ़ देखते नहीं रहते। यहीं नीचे, एक शरीर में, बाकी सबके साथ उसी मुश्किल के बीच।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In the stories of Vishnu, when the world tips too far — when something has gone so wrong that nobody inside the world can fix it — Vishnu comes down INTO the world to set it right. Not watching from above. Down here, in a body, inside the trouble with everyone else.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-what-is-an-avatar.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.what-is-an-avatar|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.what-is-an-avatar-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.what-is-an-avatar:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Word That Means Coming Down","text":"\"और यह वह बात है जिस पर बच्चे आमतौर पर सबसे पहले ध्यान देते हैं और बड़े अक्सर छोड़ देते हैं। वे हर बार किसी राजा के रूप में नहीं आते। पहली बार वे एक मछली बनते हैं। फिर एक कछुआ। फिर एक वराह। फिर शेर के सिर वाले। फिर एक छोटे बालक। और काफी बाद में, एक राजकुमार।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And here is the part children usually notice first and grown-ups usually skip. He does not come down as a king every time. The first time he is a FISH. Then a tortoise. Then a boar. A lion-headed one. A small boy. Only later, a prince.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-what-is-an-avatar.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.what-is-an-avatar|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.what-is-an-avatar-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.what-is-an-avatar:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Word That Means Coming Down","text":"\"पहले पानी का जीव, फिर पानी और ज़मीन दोनों पर रहने वाला जीव, फिर ज़मीन का जानवर, फिर आधा जानवर और आधा इंसान, फिर एक छोटा इंसान, और फिर एक पूरा इंसान। कुछ लोग ध्यान देते हैं कि यह कुछ-कुछ वैसा ही क्रम लगता है जैसे खुद ज़िंदगी की शुरुआत हुई थी। क्या कहानी सुनाने वालों का यही मतलब था, इस बात पर लोग बहस करना खूब पसंद करते हैं—पक्के तौर पर कोई नहीं कह सकता, इसलिए किसी को ऐसा जताने का ढोंग भी नहीं करना चाहिए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Water first, then a creature that lives in water and on land, then a land animal, then half-animal and half-human, then a small human, then a full one. Some people notice that this looks a little like the order life itself arrived in. Whether the storytellers meant that is something people enjoy arguing about — nobody can say for certain, so nobody should pretend to.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-what-is-an-avatar.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.what-is-an-avatar|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.what-is-an-avatar-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.what-is-an-avatar:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Word That Means Coming Down","text":"\"आमतौर पर इनकी गिनती दस मानी जाती है। दश यानी दस; अवतार यानी नीचे उतरना। दशावतार।\"","lang":"hi","body":"They are usually counted as ten. Dasha means ten; avatara means the coming-down. Dashavatara.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-what-is-an-avatar.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.what-is-an-avatar|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.what-is-an-avatar-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.what-is-an-avatar:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Word That Means Coming Down","text":"\"ज़्यादातर सूचियों में कहा जाता है: मत्स्य, कूर्म, वराह, नरसिंह, वामन, परशुराम, राम, कृष्ण, बुद्ध, कल्कि। लेकिन कई परिवार—खासकर बंगाल, ओडिशा और कई वैष्णव परंपराओं में—नौवें स्थान पर कृष्ण के बड़े भाई बलराम को गिनते हैं। कुछ लोग दोनों को गिनते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Most lists say: Matsya, Kurma, Varaha, Narasimha, Vamana, Parashurama, Rama, Krishna, the Buddha, Kalki. But many families — especially in Bengal, Odisha, and in several Vaishnava traditions — count BALARAMA, Krishna’s elder brother, in the ninth place instead. Some count both.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-what-is-an-avatar.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.what-is-an-avatar|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.what-is-an-avatar-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.what-is-an-avatar:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Word That Means Coming Down","text":"और इन कहानियों को सुनाने वाली सबसे पुरानी किताबों में से एक, भागवत पुराण, एक जगह पर इससे भी लंबी सूची देती है, और फिर एक बड़ी प्यारी बात कहती है: कि भगवान का धरती पर उतरना अनगिनत बार होता है, बिल्कुल वैसे ही जैसे किसी झील से निकलने वाली धाराओं को गिना नहीं जा सकता।","lang":"hi","body":"And one of the oldest books that tells these stories, the Bhagavata Purana, lists a much longer set in one place, and then says something lovely: that the comings-down are beyond counting, the way you cannot count the streams that come off a lake.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-what-is-an-avatar.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.what-is-an-avatar|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.matsya-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.matsya:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fish Who Kept Outgrowing the Bowl","text":"मनु नाम के एक राजा एक नदी में खड़े थे और अपने हाथों से पानी बहने दे रहे थे, तभी कोई बहुत छोटी सी चीज़ तैरकर उनकी हथेली पर आ बैठी। एक मछली, जो उनके अँगूठे से बड़ी नहीं थी।","lang":"hi","body":"A king called Manu was standing in a river, letting the water run over his hands, when something very small swam into his palm and stayed there. A fish, no longer than his thumb.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-matsya.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.matsya|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.matsya-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.matsya:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fish Who Kept Outgrowing the Bowl","text":"\"कृपया मुझे वापस मत डालिए,\" मछली ने कहा। \"बड़ी मछलियाँ छोटी मछलियों को खा जाती हैं। आप मेरी रक्षा कीजिए, और एक दिन मैं आपकी रक्षा करूँगी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Please do not put me back,\" said the fish. \"The big fish eat the small ones. Keep me safe, and one day I will keep you safe.\"","art":"art/story/sm/dv-matsya.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.matsya|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.matsya-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.matsya:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fish Who Kept Outgrowing the Bowl","text":"मनु मुस्कुराए और उसे एक छोटे से बर्तन में घर ले आए। सुबह तक मछली से वह बर्तन भर गया। उन्होंने उसे एक बड़े घड़े में डाल दिया। शाम तक वह घड़े में भी पूरी भर गई। उन्होंने उसे एक हौज़ में डाला। उसने हौज़ को भी भर दिया। वे उसे एक झील में ले गए, पर वह झील भी कम पड़ गई।","lang":"hi","body":"Manu smiled and carried it home in a little pot. By morning the fish filled the pot. He moved it to a large jar. By evening it filled the jar. He moved it to a tank. It filled the tank. He carried it to a lake, and the lake was not enough either.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-matsya.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.matsya|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.matsya-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.matsya:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fish Who Kept Outgrowing the Bowl","text":"एक छोटा बर्तन, एक घड़ा, एक हौज़, एक झील — और हर बार, जगह छोटी ही पड़ गई। भला तुम किस मोड़ पर आकर यह सोचने लगते कि आख़िर तुम अपने साथ लिए क्या घूम रहे हो?","lang":"hi","body":"A pot, a jar, a tank, a lake — and every single time, still too small. At what point would you have started to wonder what exactly you were carrying?","art":"art/story/sm/dv-matsya.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.matsya|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.matsya-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.matsya:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fish Who Kept Outgrowing the Bowl","text":"मनु आख़िरकार उसे समुद्र तक ले गए। और वहाँ वह मछली बढ़ती ही गई, यहाँ तक कि क्षितिज जितनी विशाल हो गई, उसके सिर से एक सुनहरा सींग निकल रहा था, और मनु समझ गए कि तैरकर उनके हाथों में कौन आया था।","lang":"hi","body":"Manu carried it at last to the sea. And there the fish grew until it was the size of the horizon, with a golden horn rising from its head, and Manu understood who had swum into his hands.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-matsya.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.matsya|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.matsya-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.matsya:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fish Who Kept Outgrowing the Bowl","text":"\"एक बहुत बड़ी बाढ़ आने वाली है,\" मत्स्य ने कहा। \"एक नाव बनाओ। हर पौधे के बीज, सातों ऋषि, और वह सब कुछ साथ रख लो जिसे खोना नहीं चाहिए। जब पानी चढ़ने लगे, तो अपनी नाव को मेरे सींग से बाँध देना।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"A great flood is coming,\" said Matsya. \"Build a boat. Take the seeds of every plant, and the seven sages, and whatever must not be lost. When the water rises, tie your boat to my horn.\"","art":"art/story/sm/dv-matsya.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.matsya|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.matsya-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.matsya:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Fish Who Kept Outgrowing the Bowl","text":"बारिश शुरू हो गई। नदियाँ खेतों से मिल गईं और खेत समुद्र से जा मिले, यहाँ तक कि दुनिया में कहीं कोई किनारा न बचा। और इस सबके बीच एक नाव लगातार आगे बढ़ती रही, जो एक लंबी रस्सी से सुनहरे सींग से बँधी थी, और बाद में काम आने वाली हर चीज़ उसमें सँभालकर रखी हुई थी।","lang":"hi","body":"The rain came. The rivers joined the fields, and the fields joined the sea, until there was no shore anywhere in the world. And through all of it a boat went steadily on, tied by a long rope to a golden horn, with everything that would be needed afterwards packed carefully inside.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-matsya.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.matsya|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.kurma-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.kurma:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tortoise Under the Mountain","text":"देवताओं की शक्ति घट चुकी थी। क्षीरसागर की गहराइयों में कहीं अमृत छिपा था, वह रस जो मौत को मिटा देता है — लेकिन समुद्र अपनी चीज़ें यूँ ही नहीं सौंप देता। उसे मथना पड़ता, जैसे मक्खन के लिए दूध को मथा जाता है, और किसी एक पक्ष में इतनी ताक़त नहीं थी कि वह पूरे समुद्र को मथ सके।","lang":"hi","body":"The devas had lost their strength. Somewhere at the bottom of the ocean of milk lay amrita, the nectar that ends dying — but the ocean does not simply hand things over. It would have to be churned, the way milk is churned for butter, and no one side was strong enough to churn an ocean.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-kurma.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.kurma|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.kurma-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.kurma:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tortoise Under the Mountain","text":"इसलिए देवता असुरों के पास गए। अपने सौतेले भाइयों के पास। जिनके वे हमेशा ख़िलाफ़ रहा करते थे। और असुर मान गए।","lang":"hi","body":"So the devas went to the asuras. Their half-brothers. The ones they were usually against. And the asuras said yes.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-kurma.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.kurma|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.kurma-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.kurma:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tortoise Under the Mountain","text":"मथनी के लिए उन्होंने मंदर पर्वत लिया। रस्सी के लिए उन्होंने महानाग वासुकि को लिया, जिन्हें पर्वत के चारों ओर लपेटा गया — असुरों ने सिर पकड़ा और देवों ने पूँछ। और उन्होंने खींचा, पहले एक तरफ और फिर दूसरी तरफ, और पर्वत समुद्र में घूमने लगा।","lang":"hi","body":"For a churning stick they took Mount Mandara. For a rope they took Vasuki, the great serpent, wound around the mountain — asuras holding the head, devas holding the tail. And they pulled, one side and then the other, and the mountain turned in the sea.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-kurma.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.kurma|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.kurma-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.kurma:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tortoise Under the Mountain","text":"और पर्वत डूबने लगा। उसके नीचे कुछ भी नहीं था। वह समुद्र की नरम तलहटी में धँसता जा रहा था, और यह सारी भारी मेहनत कीचड़ में मिलकर खत्म होने ही वाली थी।","lang":"hi","body":"And the mountain began to sink. There was nothing under it. It was pushing itself down into the soft floor of the ocean, and the whole enormous effort was about to end in mud.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-kurma.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.kurma|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.kurma-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.kurma:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tortoise Under the Mountain","text":"विष्णु जी कूर्म यानी एक द्वीप जितने बड़े कछुए का रूप धरकर नीचे आए, मंदर के नीचे टिक गए, और उसे थाम लिया। पर्वत का डूबना रुक गया। मंथन चलता रहा — बहुत लंबे समय तक, जहाँ नाग-रस्सी चरमरा रही थी और दोनों पक्ष पूरी ताकत से खींच रहे थे।","lang":"hi","body":"Vishnu came down as Kurma, a tortoise the size of an island, and settled under Mandara, and held. The mountain stopped sinking. The churning went on — for a very long time, with the serpent-rope creaking and both sides heaving.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-kurma.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.kurma|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.kurma-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.kurma:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tortoise Under the Mountain","text":"और समुद्र से चीज़ें बाहर आने लगीं। मनोकामना पूरी करने वाली एक गाय। एक सफ़ेद घोड़ा। एक सफ़ेद हाथी। सदा फूलों से लदा रहने वाला एक पेड़। चंद्रमा। स्वयं लक्ष्मी जी उसमें से प्रकट हुईं। और अंत में, अमृत।","lang":"hi","body":"And the ocean began to give things up. A wish-granting cow. A white horse. A white elephant. A tree that flowers forever. The moon. Lakshmi herself rose out of it. And at last, the amrita.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-kurma.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.kurma|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.kurma-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.kurma:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tortoise Under the Mountain","text":"फिर ज़ाहिर है, दोनों पक्ष सब कुछ खुद पाना चाहते थे, और उस झगड़े की अपनी ही एक कहानी है। लेकिन इस बात को याद रखिए: देव इसे अकेले नहीं कर सकते थे। असुर भी नहीं कर सकते थे। उस समुद्र से जो भी अच्छी चीज़ निकली, वह इसलिए निकली क्योंकि एक-दूसरे को नापसंद करने वाले दोनों पक्षों ने एक ही रस्सी खींची थी।","lang":"hi","body":"Then, of course, both sides wanted all of it, and that argument is a story of its own. But hold on to this bit: the devas could not do it alone. Neither could the asuras. Every good thing that came out of that ocean came out because two sides who did not like each other pulled the same rope.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-kurma.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.kurma|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.varaha-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.varaha:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boar Who Lifted the Earth","text":"हिरण्याक्ष भारी ताक़त वाला एक असुर था, और उसे अपनी ताक़त पर वैसा ही घमंड था जैसा कभी-कभी ताक़तवर लोगों को हो जाता है — वह अपनी ताक़त कहीं आज़माना चाहता था। इसलिए उसने पूरी धरती को उठाया और उसे ब्रह्मांडीय महासागर की गहराइयों में ले जाकर छोड़ दिया, और सबको चुनौती दे डाली कि कोई आकर इसे वापस ले जाए।","lang":"hi","body":"Hiranyaksha was an asura of enormous strength, and he was proud of it in the way that strong people sometimes are — he wanted somewhere to put it. So he took the whole earth and carried it down under the cosmic ocean, and left it there, and dared anyone to come and take it back.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-varaha.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.varaha|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.varaha-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.varaha:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boar Who Lifted the Earth","text":"अब ज़रा इस मुश्किल के बारे में सोचिए। धरती सतह पर नहीं है। वह बिल्कुल तलहटी में है, अंधेरे में, दुनिया भर के सारे पानी के नीचे। यहाँ आपको सिर्फ़ लड़ने वाले की ज़रूरत नहीं है। आपको किसी ऐसे की ज़रूरत है जो खोद सके।","lang":"hi","body":"Now think about the shape of that problem. The earth is not on the surface. It is at the very bottom, in the dark, under all the water there is. You do not need someone who can fight. You need someone who can DIG.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-varaha.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.varaha|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.varaha-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.varaha:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boar Who Lifted the Earth","text":"और विष्णु वराह के रूप में नीचे आए — यानी एक जंगली सूअर। यह सुनने में अजीब लग सकता है, जब तक कि आपने किसी सूअर को काम करते न देखा हो। सूअर का पूरा शरीर उसकी थूथन और उन दो दाँतों के हिसाब से बना होता है जो मिट्टी को उलट-पलट देते हैं। वे पानी में किसी फेंके हुए पत्थर की तरह तेज़ी से उतरे।","lang":"hi","body":"And Vishnu came down as Varaha — a boar. Which sounds like a strange choice until you have watched a boar work. A boar’s whole body is built around a snout and two tusks that turn earth over. He went into the water like a thrown stone.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-varaha.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.varaha|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.varaha-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.varaha:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boar Who Lifted the Earth","text":"हिरण्याक्ष नीचे उनका इंतज़ार कर रहा था, और दोनों के बीच लड़ाई हुई — एक लंबी लड़ाई, दो सचमुच के महाबलियों के बीच। यह कहानी हिरण्याक्ष का मज़ाक नहीं उड़ाती। यह कहती है कि वह एक टक्कर का विरोधी था, और सच में ऐसा ही था।","lang":"hi","body":"Hiranyaksha was waiting for him down there, and they fought — a long fight, between two who were both genuinely mighty. The story does not sneer at Hiranyaksha. It says he was a worthy opponent, and it means it.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-varaha.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.varaha|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.varaha-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.varaha:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boar Who Lifted the Earth","text":"और फिर वराह ने अपने दाँत धरती के नीचे लगाए और उसे उठा लिया। उस सारे अंधेरे पानी के बीच से, ऊपर और ऊपर, पूरी दुनिया को अपने दो दाँतों पर संभाले हुए — और फिर उसे आहिस्ता से सतह पर वहीं रख दिया, जहाँ उसकी जगह थी।","lang":"hi","body":"And then Varaha put his tusks under the earth and lifted. Up through all that dark water, up and up, with the whole world balanced on two tusks — and set it back down gently on the surface where it belonged.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-varaha.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.varaha|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.varaha-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.varaha:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boar Who Lifted the Earth","text":"आप आज भी इसे चट्टान पर तराशा हुआ देख सकते हैं। मध्य प्रदेश के उदयगिरि में लगभग सोलह सौ साल पहले चट्टान को काटकर बनाई गई वराह की एक विशाल मूर्ति है, जिसमें उन्होंने धरती को अपने कंधे पर उठाया हुआ है। लोग बहुत पुराने ज़माने से यह कहानी सुनाते आ रहे हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"You can still see this one carved into rock. At Udayagiri in Madhya Pradesh there is a Varaha cut into a cliff about sixteen hundred years ago, huge, with the earth lifted on his shoulder. People have been telling this story for a very long time.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-varaha.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.varaha|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.narasimha-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.narasimha:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Not Day, Not Night, Not Inside, Not Outside","text":"हिरण्यकशिपु असुरों का एक सम्राट था, और बहुत लंबी कोशिशों के बाद उसे एक वरदान मिला — और उसने वरदान के शब्दों को वाकई बहुत सोच-समझकर चुना था। उसने माँगा कि वह न दिन में मारा जाए और न रात में; न घर के अंदर और न बाहर; न ज़मीन पर और न आकाश में; न मनुष्य के हाथों और न पशु के; और न ही किसी अस्त्र-शस्त्र से।","lang":"hi","body":"Hiranyakashipu was an emperor of the asuras, and after long, long effort he was granted a boon — and he had thought about the wording very carefully indeed. He asked that he not be killed by day nor by night; not indoors nor outdoors; not on the ground nor in the sky; not by man nor by animal; not by any weapon.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-narasimha.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.narasimha|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.narasimha-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.narasimha:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Not Day, Not Night, Not Inside, Not Outside","text":"इसे फिर से पढ़िए। यह कोई मूर्खता भरी इच्छा नहीं है। यह बहुत ही चतुराई भरी है — उसने वह हर दरवाज़ा बंद कर दिया था जो वह सोच सकता था। और यही बात तो इस कहानी को दिलचस्प बनाती है।","lang":"hi","body":"Read that again. It is not a stupid wish. It is a very clever one — he has closed every door he can think of. Which is exactly what makes the story interesting.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-narasimha.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.narasimha|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.narasimha-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.narasimha:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Not Day, Not Night, Not Inside, Not Outside","text":"और फिर उसका अपना छोटा बेटा, प्रह्लाद, विष्णु भगवान से प्रेम करने लगा। चुपचाप, पूरी तरह से, और बिना किसी बहस के। उसके पिता को यह बात समझ नहीं आ रही थी, और जितना उन्होंने बालक के मन से इसे निकालने की कोशिश की, बालक उतना ही शांत होता गया।","lang":"hi","body":"And then his own small son, Prahlada, turned out to love Vishnu. Quietly, completely, and without any argument about it. His father could not understand it, and the more he tried to shake it out of the boy the calmer the boy became.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-narasimha.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.narasimha|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.narasimha-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.narasimha:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Not Day, Not Night, Not Inside, Not Outside","text":"\"तो फिर कहाँ हैं तुम्हारे ये विष्णु?\" आख़िरकार गुस्से में आकर उसके पिता ने पूछा। \"दिखाओ मुझे। क्या वे इस सभा-भवन में हैं? क्या वे इस खंभे में हैं?\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Where is this Vishnu of yours, then?\" his father demanded at last, furious. \"Show me. Is he in this hall? Is he in this pillar?\"","art":"art/story/sm/dv-narasimha.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.narasimha|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.narasimha-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.narasimha:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Not Day, Not Night, Not Inside, Not Outside","text":"\"वे खंभे में हैं,\" प्रह्लाद ने कहा। \"वे हर जगह हैं। ऐसी कोई जगह नहीं जहाँ वे न हों।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"He is in the pillar,\" said Prahlada. \"He is everywhere. There is nowhere he is not.\"","art":"art/story/sm/dv-narasimha.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.narasimha|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.narasimha-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.narasimha:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Not Day, Not Night, Not Inside, Not Outside","text":"सम्राट ने खंभे पर वार किया। और उसमें से एक ऐसा रूप निकलकर आया जो न इंसान था और न जानवर — इंसान के धड़ पर शेर का सिर, नरसिंह। उन्होंने हिरण्यकशिपु को गोधूलि के समय पकड़ा, जो न दिन है और न रात। चौखट पर, जो न घर के अंदर है और न बाहर। अपनी गोद में, जो न ज़मीन है और न आसमान। अपने नाखूनों से, जो कोई हथियार नहीं हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The emperor struck the pillar. And out of it came a form that was neither a man nor an animal — a lion’s head on a man’s body, Narasimha. He took Hiranyakashipu at twilight, which is not day and not night. On a threshold, which is not indoors and not outdoors. Across his lap, which is not the ground and not the sky. With his claws, which are not a weapon.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-narasimha.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.narasimha|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.narasimha-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.narasimha:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Not Day, Not Night, Not Inside, Not Outside","text":"हर एक बंद दरवाज़ा, और कहानी उनके बीच की जगह से निकल जाती है। इसीलिए बच्चों को यह बात याद रहती है — यह एक पहेली है, और पहेली ही तो पूरी बात है।","lang":"hi","body":"Every single door, and the story walks through the gap between them. That is why children remember this one — it is a riddle, and the riddle is the whole point.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-narasimha.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.narasimha|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.narasimha-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.narasimha:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Not Day, Not Night, Not Inside, Not Outside","text":"और फिर वह भयानक रूप शांत हो गया, क्योंकि प्रह्लाद बिना डरे उनके सामने आकर खड़ा हो गया। कहानियाँ कहती हैं कि उस बालक की शांति ही अकेली ऐसी चीज़ थी जिसने उन्हें शांत किया। नरसिंह को रक्षक के रूप में पूजा जाता है — वे जो तब आते हैं जब कोई वचन निभाना हो।","lang":"hi","body":"And then the terrible form went quiet, because Prahlada came and stood in front of it, unafraid. The stories say the boy’s calm was the only thing that settled him. Narasimha is worshipped as a protector — the one who arrives when a promise has to be kept.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-narasimha.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.narasimha|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.vamana-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.vamana:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Steps, and a King Who Kept His Word","text":"महाबली एक असुर राजा थे, और वे बहुत अच्छे राजा थे। यह इस कहानी का कोई नया मोड़ नहीं है; यह तो इसकी शुरुआत है। बली के राज में कोई झूठ नहीं बोलता था, कोई भूखा नहीं था, किसी के साथ धोखा नहीं होता था, और कोई दरवाज़े पर ताला नहीं लगाता था। उनकी प्रजा उनसे बेहद प्यार करती थी। वे आज भी करते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Mahabali was an asura king, and he was a good one. That is not a twist in this story; it is the starting point. Under Bali nobody lied, nobody was hungry, nobody was cheated, and nobody locked a door. His people adored him. They still do.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-vamana.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.vamana|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.vamana-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.vamana:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Steps, and a King Who Kept His Word","text":"वे उस समय के सबसे बड़े दानवीर भी थे। उन्होंने एक प्रतिज्ञा ली थी: अपने महायज्ञ में, जो कोई भी उनसे कुछ माँगेगा, उसे वह मिलेगा। कुछ भी। वे एक भी व्यक्ति को खाली हाथ नहीं लौटाएँगे।","lang":"hi","body":"He was also the most generous man alive. He had made a vow: at his great sacrifice, whoever asked him for anything would get it. Anything. He would not send a single person away.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-vamana.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.vamana|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.vamana-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.vamana:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Steps, and a King Who Kept His Word","text":"और यज्ञ में लकड़ी की छतरी थामे एक छोटा ब्राह्मण बालक चलकर आया। वामन। उसने तीन पग ज़मीन माँगी — बस उतनी ज़मीन, जितनी वह तीन कदमों में नाप सके।","lang":"hi","body":"And into the sacrifice walked a small brahmin boy, carrying a wooden umbrella. Vamana. He asked for three paces of land — as much ground as he could cover in three steps.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-vamana.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.vamana|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.vamana-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.vamana:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Steps, and a King Who Kept His Word","text":"बलि के गुरु, महान गुरु शुक्राचार्य ने देखा कि उनके सामने कौन खड़ा है, और उनका चेहरा सफ़ेद पड़ गया। \"महाराज! इन्हें वचन मत दीजिए। यह कोई बालक नहीं हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Bali’s teacher, the great guru Shukracharya, saw what was standing in front of them and went white. \"My king. Do not promise this one. That is not a child.\"","art":"art/story/sm/dv-vamana.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.vamana|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.vamana-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.vamana:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Steps, and a King Who Kept His Word","text":"\"इन्होंने माँगा है,\" बलि ने कहा। \"और मैंने वचन दिया था कि जो भी माँगेगा, उसे मिलेगा। गुरुजी — अगर मैं तीन पग माँगने वाले एक छोटे से बालक को दिया अपना वचन तोड़ दूँ, तो इतने बरसों से आख़िर मैं था ही क्या?\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"He has asked,\" said Bali. \"And I said that whoever asks will receive. Guruji — if I break my word to a small boy asking for three steps, what exactly have I been all these years?\"","art":"art/story/sm/dv-vamana.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.vamana|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.vamana-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.vamana:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Steps, and a King Who Kept His Word","text":"तो बलि ने दान का संकल्प पक्का करने के लिए हाथ से जल छोड़ा। और वह छोटा बालक बढ़ने लगा। एक पग में पूरी धरती नाप ली। दूसरे पग में पूरा आकाश नाप लिया। और तीसरे पग के लिए कहीं कोई जगह ही नहीं बची।","lang":"hi","body":"So Bali poured the water that seals a gift. And the small boy began to grow. One step covered the whole earth. The second step covered the whole sky. And there was nowhere left for the third.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-vamana.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.vamana|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.vamana-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.vamana:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Steps, and a King Who Kept His Word","text":"बलि ने न तो कोई बहस की, और न वे भागे। वे घुटनों के बल बैठे, उन्होंने अपना सिर झुकाया, और कहा: \"एक जगह अब भी बची है। अपना तीसरा पग यहाँ रखिए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Bali did not argue, and he did not run. He knelt, and he bowed his head, and he said: \"There is one place left. Put your third step here.\"","art":"art/story/sm/dv-vamana.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.vamana|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.vamana-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.vamana:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Steps, and a King Who Kept His Word","text":"और यही — न कि उनका विशाल रूप लेना, न वे दो विशाल कदम — वह पल है जिस पर यह पूरी कहानी रची गई है। उनसे धोखे से वचन पूरा नहीं करवाया गया था। उन्होंने सब कुछ जानते हुए भी अपना वचन निभाया।","lang":"hi","body":"And that — not the growing, not the two enormous steps — is the moment the whole story is built around. He was not tricked into keeping his word. He kept it after he knew.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-vamana.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.vamana|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.vamana-8":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.vamana:8","title":"Read it in Hindi · Three Steps, and a King Who Kept His Word","text":"तो वामन ने बलि के सिर पर अपना पैर रखा और उन्हें एक दूसरे लोक पर राज करने के लिए नीचे भेज दिया। लेकिन उन्होंने उन्हें एक वरदान दिया: हर साल एक बार, महाबलि अपने घर आकर अपनी प्रजा से मिल सकते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"So Vamana set his foot on Bali’s head and sent him down to rule another realm. But he granted him one thing: once every year, Mahabali may come home and see his people.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-vamana.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.vamana|h8","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.parashurama-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.parashurama:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sage Who Carried an Axe","text":"परशुराम का जन्म ऋषियों के परिवार में हुआ था, और वे किसी भी और चीज़ से पहले एक विद्वान थे। जिस कुल्हाड़ी के नाम पर उनका नाम पड़ा — परशु — वह उन्हें भगवान शिव ने दी थी। यह एक अनोखा मेल है, और कहानियाँ भी यह बात जानती हैं: एक ऐसा इंसान जिसे सोचना-समझना सिखाया गया हो, हाथ में हथियार थामे हुए।","lang":"hi","body":"Parashurama was born into a family of sages, and he was a scholar before he was anything else. The axe he is named for — parashu — was given to him by Shiva. That is an unusual combination, and the stories know it: a man trained to think, holding a weapon.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-parashurama.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.parashurama|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.parashurama-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.parashurama:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sage Who Carried an Axe","text":"उनके ज़माने के राजाओं ने जिसके पास जो कुछ था, उससे अपनी मनमर्ज़ी से छीनना शुरू कर दिया था। उनमें से एक ने उनके परिवार को लूटा और उनके पिता की जान ले ली। और परशुराम, जिन्हें शब्दों से तर्क करना सिखाया गया था, उन्होंने उसकी जगह कुल्हाड़ी उठा ली।","lang":"hi","body":"Kings in his time had begun to take whatever they wanted from whoever had it. One of them robbed his family and killed his father. And Parashurama, who had been raised to argue with words, picked up the axe instead.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-parashurama.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.parashurama|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.parashurama-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.parashurama:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sage Who Carried an Axe","text":"इसके बाद दशावतार का वह हिस्सा आता है जिसे बड़े लोग बहुत संभलकर सुनाते हैं, और मैं भी इसे उसी तरह सुनाने जा रहा हूँ। वे बहुत लंबे समय तक उन राजाओं के पीछे पड़े रहे। कहानियाँ यह नहीं कहतीं कि वे सही थे। वे बस यह कहती हैं कि वे खुद को रोक नहीं पाए।","lang":"hi","body":"What follows is the part of the Dashavatara that grown-ups tell most carefully, and I am going to tell it the same way. He went after those kings for a very long time. The stories do not say he was right. They say he could not stop.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-parashurama.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.parashurama|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.parashurama-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.parashurama:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sage Who Carried an Axe","text":"आखिरकार उनके अपने गुरुओं ने उन्हें वही बात समझाई जो वे पहले से जानते थे: कि गुस्सा, भले ही न्याय की खातिर शुरू हुआ हो, कुछ समय बाद अपना ही रूप ले लेता है और उस वजह को सुनना बंद कर देता है जिससे वह शुरू हुआ था।","lang":"hi","body":"His own teachers eventually told him what he already knew: that anger, even anger that began as justice, becomes its own thing after a while and stops listening to the reason that started it.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-parashurama.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.parashurama|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.parashurama-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.parashurama:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sage Who Carried an Axe","text":"तो वे रुक गए। उन्होंने वह सारी ज़मीन दान कर दी जो उन्होंने जीती थी — उसका एक-एक खेत — और पहाड़ों में चले गए, और अपनी उस बेहद लंबी ज़िंदगी का बाकी हिस्सा सिखाने-पढ़ाने में बिताया। वे उन लोगों में से हैं जिनके बारे में कहानियाँ कहती हैं कि वे कभी मरे नहीं। वे बस कहीं हैं, आज भी, एकदम शांत।","lang":"hi","body":"So he stopped. He gave away all the land he had taken — every last field of it — and went to the mountains, and spent the rest of an extremely long life teaching. He is one of the ones the stories say has not died. He is simply somewhere, still, being quiet.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-parashurama.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.parashurama|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.parashurama-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.parashurama:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sage Who Carried an Axe","text":"पश्चिमी तट पर — केरल में, कोंकण में, गोवा में — पुरानी मान्यताएँ कहती हैं कि परशुराम ने अपनी कुल्हाड़ी समुद्र में फेंकी और समुद्र पीछे हट गया, और वही वह ज़मीन है जिस पर वहाँ के लोग रहते हैं। समुद्र किनारे रहने वाले परिवार सदियों से अपनी धरती के बारे में यही कहानी सुनाते आ रहे हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Along the western coast — in Kerala, in Konkan, in Goa — there are old traditions that say Parashurama threw his axe into the sea and the sea drew back, and that is the land people live on there. Coastal families have been telling that about their own ground for centuries.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-parashurama.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.parashurama|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.rama-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.rama:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Seventh: the One Who Kept the Rules","text":"सातवाँ अवतार राम हैं, और उनकी कहानी इस शेल्फ़ की महज़ एक कहानी नहीं है — वह तो पूरी एक किताब है, चौबीस रातों जितनी लंबी, जो ‘रामायण’ के नाम से तुम्हारा इंतज़ार कर रही है। इसलिए यहाँ हम सिर्फ़ वही सवाल पूछेंगे जो यह किताब दसों अवतारों से पूछती है: वे किस रूप में धरती पर आए, और उसी रूप में क्यों?","lang":"hi","body":"The seventh coming-down is Rama, and his story is not a story in this shelf — it is a whole book, twenty-four nights of it, waiting for you under The Ramayana. So here we will only ask the question this collection asks of each of the ten: what shape did he come down in, and why that one?","art":"art/story/sm/dv-rama.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.rama|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.rama-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.rama:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Seventh: the One Who Kept the Rules","text":"मत्स्य एक मछली थे। कूर्म एक कछुआ। वराह एक जंगली सूअर, नरसिंह आधे शेर, वामन एक छोटे बालक जो बड़े होते चले गए। राम अलग हैं। राम पूरी तरह से, शत-प्रतिशत एक इंसान हैं। न कोई अतिरिक्त हाथ। न कोई विशाल रूप। कुछ भी ऐसा नहीं जो एक साधारण इंसान नहीं हो सकता।","lang":"hi","body":"Matsya was a fish. Kurma was a tortoise. Varaha a boar, Narasimha half a lion, Vamana a small boy who grew. Rama is different. Rama is entirely, completely a man. No extra arms. No growing. Nothing that a person could not be.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-rama.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.rama|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.rama-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.rama:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Seventh: the One Who Kept the Rules","text":"और पूरी कहानी इसी बात पर टिकी है। पिता के दिए एक वचन की वजह से उन्हें चौदह साल के लिए जंगल जाने को कहा जाता है, और वे चले जाते हैं — जैसे कोई इंसान जाता है, पैदल, बिना कुछ लिए। वे ऊपर से बैठकर सब ठीक नहीं करते। वे ख़ुद उस राह पर चलकर जाते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"And the whole story turns on that. He is asked to go into the forest for fourteen years by a promise his father made, and he goes — as a man goes, on foot, with nothing. He does not fix it from above. He walks it.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-rama.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.rama|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.rama-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.rama:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Seventh: the One Who Kept the Rules","text":"\"लोग उनके लिए जो शब्द इस्तेमाल करते हैं, वह है मर्यादा — यानी सही सीमा, वह लकीर जिसके भीतर रहा जाए। मर्यादा पुरुषोत्तम: वह जिन्होंने हमेशा मर्यादा का पालन किया। यह शब्द ताक़त के बारे में बिल्कुल नहीं है। यह संयम के बारे में है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The word people use for him is maryada — the proper limit, the line you keep to. Maryada Purushottama: the one who kept within the line. It is not a word about power at all. It is a word about restraint.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-rama.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.rama|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.krishna-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.krishna:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Eighth: the One Who Would Not Be Serious","text":"\"आठवें अवतार एक नन्हे बच्चे के रूप में धरती पर आते हैं, एक जेल में, मूसलाधार बारिश की रात में, और उन्हें उफनती नदी पार कराकर सुरक्षित रूप से ग्वालों के गाँव पहुँचाया जाता है। और फिर वे कुछ ऐसा करते हैं जो बाकी किसी ने नहीं किया। वे बच्चे ही बने रहते हैं, और बड़े नटखट होते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The eighth comes down as a baby, in a prison, on a night of pouring rain, and is carried across a flooded river to safety in a cowherd village. And then he does something none of the others do. He stays a child, and he is naughty.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-krishna.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.krishna|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.krishna-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.krishna:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Eighth: the One Who Would Not Be Serious","text":"\"यह सचमुच बड़ा अनोखा है। मत्स्य खेलते नहीं हैं। कूर्म किसी को नहीं छेड़ते। लेकिन कृष्ण माखन चुराते हैं, बछड़ों को खोल देते हैं, गोपियों के कपड़े पेड़ पर छिपा देते हैं, और लगातार पकड़े जाते हैं और हर बार माफ़ भी कर दिए जाते हैं। गीतों के पूरे के पूरे ग्रंथ सिर्फ़ इसी बारे में हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"That is genuinely unusual. Matsya does not play. Kurma does not tease anyone. But Krishna steals butter, unties calves, hides the milkmaids’ clothes in a tree, and is caught constantly and forgiven constantly. Whole libraries of songs are about nothing but this.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-krishna.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.krishna|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.krishna-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.krishna:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Eighth: the One Who Would Not Be Serious","text":"\"जब गाँव वाले वर्षा के देवता, इंद्र के लिए अपनी हमेशा वाली बड़ी पूजा करने जा रहे थे, तो कृष्ण ने पूछा कि ऐसा क्यों? उस पहाड़ी की पूजा क्यों नहीं, जो सचमुच गायों का पेट भरती है, और ख़ुद गायों की क्यों नहीं? तो उन्होंने वैसा ही किया — और इंद्र ने ख़ुद को अपमानित मानकर, उन्हें डुबोने के लिए एक भयंकर तूफ़ान भेज दिया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"When the village was going to hold its usual grand offering to Indra, the deva of rain, Krishna asked why. Why not to the hill that actually feeds the cows, and the cows themselves? So they did — and Indra, insulted, sent a storm to drown them.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-krishna.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.krishna|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.krishna-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.krishna:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Eighth: the One Who Would Not Be Serious","text":"\"और एक बालक ने गोवर्धन पर्वत को अपनी एक उँगली पर उठा लिया और सात दिनों तक उसे छाते की तरह थामे रखा, और हर कोई — हर इंसान, हर गाय — उसके नीचे खड़ा रहा और भीगने से बच गया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And a boy lifted the hill Govardhan on one finger and held it up like an umbrella for seven days, and everyone — every person, every cow — stood under it and stayed dry.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-krishna.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.krishna|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.krishna-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.krishna:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Eighth: the One Who Would Not Be Serious","text":"वे बड़े होते हैं। वे गाँव छोड़ देते हैं, जिसका अपना एक दुःख है और अपने ही गीत हैं। वे गुजरात के समुद्र तट पर द्वारका नगरी बसाते हैं। और महाभारत में तो वे लड़ने से साफ़ मना कर देते हैं — इसके बजाय वे अर्जुन का रथ हाँकते हैं, उनसे बातें करते हैं, और वही बातचीत आगे चलकर भगवद्गीता बन गई।","lang":"hi","body":"He grows up. He leaves the village, which is its own sadness and its own set of songs. He founds a city at Dwarka on the coast of Gujarat. And in the Mahabharata he refuses to fight at all — he drives Arjuna’s chariot instead, and talks to him, and that conversation became the Bhagavad Gita.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-krishna.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.krishna|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.krishna-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.krishna:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Eighth: the One Who Would Not Be Serious","text":"नन्हे बालक, चोर, पहाड़ उठाने वाले, बाँसुरी बजाने वाले, दोस्त, सारथी, गुरु। ये ऐसे पड़ाव नहीं हैं जिनसे वे गुज़रे और उन्हें पीछे छोड़ आए — आज भी, अलग-अलग घरों में और अलग-अलग राज्यों में, लोग एक ही समय पर उनके हर एक रूप की पूजा करते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Baby, thief, hill-lifter, flute player, friend, charioteer, teacher. Not stages he passed through and left behind — people worship every one of them at the same time, in different houses, in different states, today.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-krishna.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.krishna|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.kalki-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.kalki:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tenth, Who Has Not Come Yet","text":"इस किताब में तुमने जो भी कहानी पढ़ी है, वह कथा के अनुसार घट चुकी है — एक मछली आई, एक कछुए ने सहारा दिया, एक बालक ने तीन डग भरे। यह वाली अभी नहीं घटी है। दसवाँ अभी आगे आना बाकी है।","lang":"hi","body":"Every story you have read in this collection happened, in the telling — a fish came, a tortoise held, a boy took three steps. This one has not. The tenth is still ahead.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-kalki.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.kalki|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.kalki-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.kalki:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tenth, Who Has Not Come Yet","text":"कल्कि के बारे में कहा जाता है कि वे एक लंबे, थके हुए युग के अंत में, एक सफ़ेद घोड़े पर, एक चमकती तलवार के साथ आएँगे — जो कुछ गलत हुआ है उसे खत्म करने और सब कुछ नए सिरे से, पूरी तरह साफ़-सुथरा शुरू करने के लिए।","lang":"hi","body":"Kalki is spoken of as arriving at the end of a long, tired age, on a white horse, with a bright sword — to end what has gone wrong and start the whole thing over, clean.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-kalki.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.kalki|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.kalki-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.kalki:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tenth, Who Has Not Come Yet","text":"और अब मुझे तुम्हारे साथ ज़रा संभलकर रहना होगा, क्योंकि यह बिल्कुल वैसी कहानी है जिसमें लोगों का मन कुछ न कुछ अपनी तरफ़ से जोड़ने को करता है। यह कब की बात है? कोई नहीं जानता। परंपरा में कोई तारीख तय नहीं है, और मैं भी तुम्हारे लिए कोई मनगढ़ंत तारीख नहीं बनाने वाला। जो भी तुमसे कहे कि उसे साल पता है, वह तुम्हें ऐसी बात बता रहा है जो कहानियों में नहीं कही गई है।","lang":"hi","body":"And now I have to be careful with you, because this is exactly the sort of story people are tempted to add to. When is it? Nobody knows. The tradition does not fix a date, and I am not going to invent one for you. Anyone who tells you they know the year is telling you something the stories do not say.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-kalki.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.kalki|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.kalki-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.kalki:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tenth, Who Has Not Come Yet","text":"कहानियों में जिस बात का वर्णन ज़रूर मिलता है, वह है उनके आने से पहले का दौर: एक ऐसा समय जब वादों की कोई ख़ास अहमियत नहीं रह जाती, जब लोग देने से ज़्यादा लेने लगते हैं, जब ताक़तवर लोगों को यह लगना बंद हो जाता है कि किसी के प्रति उनकी कोई ज़िम्मेदारी भी है।","lang":"hi","body":"What the stories do describe is the age before he comes: a time when promises stop meaning much, when people take more than they give, when the strong stop feeling they owe anybody anything.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-kalki.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.kalki|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-dv.kalki-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:dv.kalki:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tenth, Who Has Not Come Yet","text":"दस बार नीचे उतरना। एक मछली, एक कछुआ, एक वराह, एक सिंह-रूप, एक नन्हा बालक, कुल्हाड़ी लिए एक मुनि, अपनी बात का पक्का एक राजकुमार, एक ऐसा बच्चा जो कभी गंभीर नहीं रहता था, एक नौवाँ जिसे अलग-अलग परिवार अलग-अलग तरह से गिनते हैं — और एक जिसका आना अभी बाकी है, सफ़ेद घोड़े पर, एक ऐसे समय में जिसके बारे में किसी को नहीं बताया गया है।","lang":"hi","body":"Ten comings-down. A fish, a tortoise, a boar, a lion-form, a small boy, a sage with an axe, a prince who kept his word, a child who would not be solemn, a ninth that different families count differently — and one still to come, on a white horse, at a time nobody has been told.","art":"art/story/sm/dv-kalki.jpg","route":"#/story/dv.kalki|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Ten Avatars"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.who-are-the-asuras-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.who-are-the-asuras:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Word That Does Not Mean Demon","text":"\"तुम कहानियों का एक ऐसा पूरा पिटारा पढ़ने जा रहे हो जहाँ देव और असुर आमने-सामने हैं। तो सबसे पहले, एक बात साफ़ कर लेते हैं — क्योंकि अगर तुमने इसे गलत समझ लिया, तो उसके बाद की हर कहानी गलत समझ में आएगी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"You are about to read a shelf of stories where devas and asuras are on opposite sides. So before anything else, one correction — because if you get this wrong, every story afterwards goes wrong with it.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-who-are-the-asuras.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.who-are-the-asuras|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.who-are-the-asuras-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.who-are-the-asuras:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Word That Does Not Mean Demon","text":"\"असुर का मतलब राक्षस नहीं होता। कभी था भी नहीं। इन कहानियों में देव और असुर सौतेले भाई हैं — पिता एक ही हैं, कश्यप, बस माताएँ अलग-अलग हैं। एक ही परिवार। वे ऐसे भाई हैं जो एक ही घर के लिए आपस में झगड़ रहे हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Asura does not mean demon. It never did. In the stories the devas and the asuras are HALF-BROTHERS — the same father, Kashyapa, different mothers. Same family. They are cousins arguing over the same house.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-who-are-the-asuras.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.who-are-the-asuras|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.who-are-the-asuras-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.who-are-the-asuras:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Word That Does Not Mean Demon","text":"\"जब जीवन के अमृत के लिए समुद्र को मथना था, तो कोई भी पक्ष इसे अकेले नहीं कर सकता था। इसलिए उन्होंने मिलकर यह काम किया — असुरों ने साँप का फन पकड़ा, देवों ने पूँछ पकड़ी, और बहुत देर तक उसी एक रस्सी को खींचा। उस समुद्र से जो भी अच्छी चीज़ें निकलीं, वे सिर्फ़ इसलिए निकलीं क्योंकि दोनों ने मिलकर काम किया था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"When the ocean had to be churned for the nectar of life, neither side could do it alone. So they did it together — asuras holding the serpent’s head, devas holding the tail, pulling the same rope for a very long time. Everything good that came out of that ocean came out because they worked together.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-who-are-the-asuras.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.who-are-the-asuras|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.who-are-the-asuras-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.who-are-the-asuras:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Word That Does Not Mean Demon","text":"\"और ज़रा देखो कि और कौन-कौन असुर है। एक असुर सम्राट के घर जन्मे प्रह्लाद, पूरी परंपरा में सबसे प्यारे भक्तों में से एक हैं। असुर राजा महाबली का हर ओणम पर केरल में फूलों के साथ घर वापसी पर स्वागत किया जाता है। और खुद असुरों के गुरु शुक्राचार्य एक महान और पूजनीय ऋषि हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And look who else is an asura. Prahlada, born to an asura emperor, is one of the best-loved devotees in the entire tradition. Mahabali, an asura king, is welcomed home to Kerala with flowers every single Onam. Shukracharya, the asuras’ own guru, is a great and revered sage.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-who-are-the-asuras.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.who-are-the-asuras|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.who-are-the-asuras-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.who-are-the-asuras:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Word That Does Not Mean Demon","text":"\"देव भी कोई सीधे-सादे भले लोग नहीं हैं, और कहानियाँ यह बात साफ़-साफ़ बताने से ज़रा भी नहीं कतरातीं। देवों के राजा इंद्र को घमंड हो जाता है, जलन होती है, अपनी आहत शान में वे एक गाँव पर तूफ़ान भेज देते हैं, और फिर उन्हें डाँट खानी पड़ती है। ऐसी कई कहानियों में वे ग़लत होते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The devas are not simply the good ones either, and the stories are quite happy to say so. Indra, king of the devas, gets proud, gets jealous, sends a storm at a village out of wounded pride, and has to be told off. He is in several of these stories being wrong.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-who-are-the-asuras.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.who-are-the-asuras|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.samudra-manthan-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.samudra-manthan:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Day Both Sides Pulled the Same Rope","text":"\"देवताओं की शक्ति चली गई थी — कहानियों में इसके अलग-अलग कारण मिलते हैं, और हर सुनाने वाले की अपनी एक पसंदीदा कहानी होती है। पर सभी एक ही उपाय पर सहमत हैं: क्षीरसागर की तलहटी में अमृत छिपा था, ऐसा रस जो मौत को मिटा दे। और सागर सिर्फ़ माँगने भर से तो कुछ देता नहीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The devas had lost their strength — the stories give different reasons, and every teller has a favourite. What they agree on is the fix: at the bottom of the ocean of milk lay amrita, the nectar that ends dying. And an ocean does not give things up for the asking.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-samudra-manthan.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.samudra-manthan|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.samudra-manthan-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.samudra-manthan:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Day Both Sides Pulled the Same Rope","text":"\"उसे मथना ही पड़ता, बिल्कुल वैसे ही जैसे मक्खन के लिए दूध की मटकी मथी जाती है — पर यहाँ मटकी पूरा सागर था, और अकेले किसी एक के पास इतने हाथ नहीं थे। इसलिए देवता असुरों के पास गए और उनसे पूछा। और असुर भी कोई मूर्ख तो थे नहीं, उन्हें इसमें अपना फ़ायदा दिख रहा था, सो वे मान गए।\"","lang":"hi","body":"It would have to be churned, the way a pot of milk is churned for butter — but the pot was an ocean, and no one side had the arms for it. So the devas went to the asuras and asked. And the asuras, who were not fools and could see a share in it, said yes.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-samudra-manthan.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.samudra-manthan|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.samudra-manthan-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.samudra-manthan:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Day Both Sides Pulled the Same Rope","text":"\"मथानी बना मंदार पर्वत। और रस्सी की तरह उसके चारों ओर लिपटे महानाग वासुकि। असुरों ने फन की तरफ़ से पकड़ा, देवताओं ने पूँछ थामी, और वे खींचने लगे — पहले एक तरफ़, फिर दूसरी तरफ़, फिर से पहली तरफ़, और समुद्र में पर्वत घूमने लगा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Mount Mandara for the churning stick. Vasuki the great serpent wound round it for the rope. Asuras took the head, devas took the tail, and they hauled — one side, then the other, then the first again, and the mountain turned in the sea.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-samudra-manthan.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.samudra-manthan|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.samudra-manthan-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.samudra-manthan:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Day Both Sides Pulled the Same Rope","text":"\"ज़ाहिर है, वह सीधा समुद्र की नरम तलहटी में धँसने लगा, तब भगवान विष्णु कूर्म यानी कछुआ बनकर नीचे आए और पर्वत को अपनी पीठ पर सँभाल लिया ताकि काम चलता रहे। वह अपने आप में एक अलग कहानी है और 'द टेन अवतार्ज़' में आती है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"It sank, of course, straight into the soft floor of the ocean, and Vishnu came down as Kurma the tortoise and held it up on his shell so the work could go on. That is a story of its own and it is in The Ten Avatars.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-samudra-manthan.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.samudra-manthan|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.samudra-manthan-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.samudra-manthan:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Day Both Sides Pulled the Same Rope","text":"\"और फिर, किसी भी ख़ज़ाने के निकलने से पहले, समुद्र से कुछ ऐसा निकला जो किसी को नहीं चाहिए था। हलाहल — ऐसा भयानक विष कि वह हर चीज़ में फैलने लगा। और यह पूरा भारी-भरकम काम, जो दुनिया को बचाने के लिए था, उसी दुनिया को ख़त्म करने की कगार पर पहुँच गया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And then, before any treasure at all, the ocean gave up something nobody wanted. Halahala — a poison so terrible it began to spread through everything. And the whole enormous project was about to kill the world it was meant to save.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-samudra-manthan.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.samudra-manthan|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.samudra-manthan-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.samudra-manthan:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Day Both Sides Pulled the Same Rope","text":"\"ध्यान दीजिए कि भगवान शिव इस पूरे मामले में किसी भी तरफ़ नहीं हैं। वे अपने किसी हिस्से के लिए मंथन नहीं कर रहे। वे बस आते हैं, पूरी कहानी की सबसे ख़तरनाक चीज़ को निगल जाते हैं, और बाद में इस बारे में कुछ नहीं कहते।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Notice that Shiva is not on either side of this argument. He is not churning for a share. He simply arrives, swallows the worst thing in the story, and says nothing about it afterwards.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-samudra-manthan.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.samudra-manthan|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.samudra-manthan-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.samudra-manthan:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Day Both Sides Pulled the Same Rope","text":"\"इसके बाद, समुद्र ने देना शुरू किया। मनचाहा वरदान देने वाली गाय कामधेनु। सफ़ेद घोड़ा उच्चैःश्रवा। सफ़ेद हाथी ऐरावत। पारिजात का पेड़, जिस पर फूल खिलना कभी बंद नहीं होते। चंद्रमा। धन्वंतरि, जो दुनिया में दवाइयाँ लेकर आए। और स्वयं लक्ष्मी, कमल पर प्रकट होती हुईं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"After that, the ocean began to give. Kamadhenu the wish-granting cow. Uchaishravas the white horse. Airavata the white elephant. The parijata tree that never stops flowering. The moon. Dhanvantari, who brought medicine into the world. And Lakshmi herself, rising on a lotus.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-samudra-manthan.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.samudra-manthan|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.samudra-manthan-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.samudra-manthan:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Day Both Sides Pulled the Same Rope","text":"\"और सबसे अंत में, अमृत। और दोनों पक्ष, जिन्होंने युगों तक एक ही रस्सी को खींचा था, तुरंत उसके लिए आपस में लड़ने लगे — जो किसी और पन्ने की कहानी है, और इसमें किसी की भी कोई ख़ास तारीफ़ नहीं बनती।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And at the very end, the amrita. And both sides, who had pulled the same rope for an age, immediately began to fight over it — which is a story for another page, and not a flattering one for anybody.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-samudra-manthan.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.samudra-manthan|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.prahlada-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.prahlada:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy Who Would Not Change His Mind","text":"\"हिरण्यकशिपु ने खुद को ऐसा बना लिया था कि उसे नुकसान पहुँचाना लगभग नामुमकिन था, और उसने राज भी उसी हिसाब से किया। उसके साम्राज्य में बाकी सब नियमों से ऊपर एक नियम था: विष्णु का नाम नहीं लिया जाएगा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Hiranyakashipu had made himself very nearly impossible to harm, and he ruled accordingly. There was one rule above all others in his empire: the name of Vishnu was not to be spoken.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-prahlada.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.prahlada|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.prahlada-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.prahlada:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy Who Would Not Change His Mind","text":"\"और उसके अपने ही बेटे ने वह नाम लिया। परेशान करने के लिए नहीं। प्रह्लाद को तो बस बचपन से ही विष्णु से प्रेम था, ठीक वैसे ही जैसे कुछ बच्चों को बिना किसी के सिखाए ही किसी चीज़ से प्यार हो जाता है — और जब उससे इस बारे में पूछा गया, तो उसने सच बता दिया, क्योंकि उसने अभी यह नहीं सीखा था कि सच कभी-कभी ख़तरनाक भी हो सकता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And his own son said it. Not to be difficult. Prahlada simply loved Vishnu, from very small, the way some children love something before anybody teaches them to — and when he was asked about it he told the truth, because he had not yet learned that truth is sometimes dangerous.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-prahlada.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.prahlada|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.prahlada-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.prahlada:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy Who Would Not Change His Mind","text":"\"उसके पिता ने उसे दुनिया के सबसे अच्छे गुरुओं — खुद शुक्राचार्य के बेटों — के पास भेजा, ताकि वे उसकी यह आदत छुड़ा सकें। प्रह्लाद ने बड़ी विनम्रता से हर पाठ सुना, सब कुछ सीखा, और फिर भी वही नाम लेता रहा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"His father sent him to the best teachers in the world — Shukracharya’s own sons — to have it schooled out of him. Prahlada listened politely to every lesson, learned it all, and went on saying the name.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-prahlada.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.prahlada|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.prahlada-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.prahlada:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy Who Would Not Change His Mind","text":"\"इस दुनिया में सबसे ताक़तवर मैं ही हूँ,\" उसके पिता ने कहा। \"मैंने सबको हरा दिया है। तुम बस मेरा नाम क्यों नहीं ले लेते?\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"I am the strongest being alive,\" his father said. \"I have beaten everyone. Why will you not simply say MY name?\"","art":"art/story/sm/ds-prahlada.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.prahlada|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.prahlada-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.prahlada:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy Who Would Not Change His Mind","text":"\"क्योंकि आप मेरे पिता हैं और मैं आपसे प्यार करता हूँ,\" प्रह्लाद ने कहा। \"और इसलिए भी कि वे हर जगह हैं, और आप सिर्फ़ यहाँ हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Because you are my father and I love you,\" said Prahlada. \"And because he is everywhere, and you are only here.\"","art":"art/story/sm/ds-prahlada.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.prahlada|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.prahlada-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.prahlada:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy Who Would Not Change His Mind","text":"कहानियाँ कहती हैं कि उसके पिता ने बार-बार उसे डराकर रोकने की कोशिश की, और हर बार वह बालक बिल्कुल शांत रहा, और हर बार उसकी यह शांति बात न मानने से भी ज़्यादा गुस्सा दिलाती थी। कोई भी तरकीब काम नहीं कर रही थी, और कुछ काम न आना ही सबसे बुरी बात थी।","lang":"hi","body":"The stories say his father tried, over and over, to frighten him out of it, and every time the boy came through calm, and every time the calm was more infuriating than the disobedience. Nothing was working, and the not-working was the worst part.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-prahlada.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.prahlada|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.prahlada-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.prahlada:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy Who Would Not Change His Mind","text":"यह सब कैसे ख़त्म हुआ — एक खंभा, और एक ऐसा रूप जो न इंसान था न जानवर, और ऐसा समय जो न दिन था न रात — यह सब 'दस अवतार' में नरसिंह के प्रसंग में बताया गया है। यहाँ जो बात मायने रखती है, वह यह है कि उसके बाद क्या हुआ।","lang":"hi","body":"How that ends — with a pillar, and a form that is neither man nor animal, at an hour that is neither day nor night — is told in The Ten Avatars, under Narasimha. What matters here is what happened afterwards.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-prahlada.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.prahlada|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.prahlada-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.prahlada:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Boy Who Would Not Change His Mind","text":"जब उस भयानक सिंह-रूप ने वह काम कर दिया जिसके लिए वह आया था और कोई भी उसके पास नहीं जा पा रहा था, तब वह बालक ही था जो उनके पास चलकर गया। बिना किसी डर के। और कहानियाँ कहती हैं कि वह प्रह्लाद की शांति ही थी, और सिर्फ़ वही, जिसने उन्हें शांत किया।","lang":"hi","body":"When the terrible lion-form had done what it came for and nobody could go near it, it was the boy who walked up to it. Not afraid. And the stories say it was Prahlada’s calm, and only that, which settled it.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-prahlada.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.prahlada|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.tarakasura-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.tarakasura:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Only a Child Not Yet Born","text":"तारकासुर ने बड़ी चतुराई से नाप-तौलकर एक वरदान माँगा: कि उसे सिर्फ़ शिवजी का पुत्र ही हरा सके। और जिस समय उसने यह माँगा, शिवजी का कोई पुत्र नहीं था, न ही होने वाला था, और वे पहाड़ों में आँखें मूँदे, दुनिया-जहान की परवाह से कोसों दूर बैठे थे।","lang":"hi","body":"Tarakasura asked for a boon with a very neat shape to it: that he could be defeated only by a son of Shiva. And at the time he asked, Shiva had no son, was not going to have one, and was sitting in the mountains with his eyes shut, some way past caring.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-tarakasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.tarakasura|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.tarakasura-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.tarakasura:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Only a Child Not Yet Born","text":"यह बड़ी होशियारी भरी इच्छा थी। इसमें यह नहीं कहा गया कि \"मुझे कोई नहीं हरा सकता\"—ऐसी इच्छा तो फौरन खारिज कर दी जाती है। इसमें एक ऐसे व्यक्ति का नाम लिया गया जो मौजूद ही नहीं है और न कभी होने वाला है।","lang":"hi","body":"That is a clever wish. It does not say \"nobody can beat me\" — a wish like that gets refused. It names one person who does not exist and is not going to.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-tarakasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.tarakasura|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.tarakasura-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.tarakasura:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Only a Child Not Yet Born","text":"तो तारकासुर ने तीनों लोकों पर कब्ज़ा कर लिया, और देवता मदद के इकलौते दरवाज़े की तरफ दौड़े, पर वह बंद मिला। शिवजी गहरे ध्यान में लीन थे और युगों से ऐसे ही समाधि में थे।","lang":"hi","body":"So Tarakasura took the three worlds, and the devas went to look for the only door there was, and found it shut. Shiva was deep in meditation and had been for an age.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-tarakasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.tarakasura|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.tarakasura-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.tarakasura:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Only a Child Not Yet Born","text":"यह पार्वती थीं जिन्होंने इस सब को बदला, और वह भी किसी के भेजने पर नहीं। उन्होंने खुद शिवजी को चुना, वे खुद पहाड़ों पर गईं, और उन्होंने इंतज़ार किया—कड़कड़ाती ठंड, तपती धूप और बरसों के बीतने तक—एक ऐसे धैर्य के साथ जिसकी मिसाल ये कहानियाँ इस पूरी किताब में किसी के भी बल-पौरुष से कहीं ज़्यादा देती हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"It was Parvati who changed that, and not by being sent. She chose him, and she went to the mountains herself, and she waited — through cold and heat and years of it — with a patience the stories admire more than they admire anybody’s strength in this whole shelf.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-tarakasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.tarakasura|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.tarakasura-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.tarakasura:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Only a Child Not Yet Born","text":"\"और उनके बेटे थे कार्तिकेय। स्वयं शिव की अग्नि से जन्मे, जिन्हें अग्निदेव ले गए, जो गंगा में शीतल हुए, और कुछ समय के लिए छह माताओं ने जिन्हें पाला — वे छह तारे जिन्हें लोग कृत्तिका कहते हैं — जहाँ से उनका नाम आया, और इसीलिए उन्हें छह चेहरों के साथ दिखाया जाता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And their son was Kartikeya. Born from Shiva’s own fire, carried by Agni, cooled in the Ganga, raised for a while by six mothers — the six stars people call the Krittika — which is where his name comes from, and why he is shown with six faces.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-tarakasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.tarakasura|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.tarakasura-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.tarakasura:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Only a Child Not Yet Born","text":"\"देवताओं ने उन्हें अपनी सेनाओं का सेनापति बनाया, और उन्हें वेल दिया — यानी एक भाला — और वे मोर पर सवार होकर निकले और उस संकट को खत्म कर दिया जिसे उनसे बड़ा कोई छू भी नहीं पाया था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"They made him commander of the armies of the devas, and gave him the vel — a spear — and he rode out on a peacock and ended what nobody older had been able to touch.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-tarakasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.tarakasura|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.tarakasura-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.tarakasura:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Only a Child Not Yet Born","text":"\"दक्षिण में वे मुरुगन हैं, और वहाँ वे कोई साधारण रूप नहीं हैं — वे सबके सबसे प्रिय हैं। तमिलनाडु के छह बड़े मंदिर, यानी 'आरुपदै वीडु', उनके धाम हैं, और लोग कावड़ी लेकर पैदल उन तक जाते हैं। स्कंद, सुब्रह्मण्य, षण्मुख, कार्तिकेय, मुरुगन: ये सब वही एक युवा सेनापति हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In the south he is Murugan, and he is not a minor figure there at all — he is one of the most loved of all. Six great temples in Tamil Nadu, the Arupadai Veedu, are his houses, and people walk to them carrying kavadi. Skanda, Subramanya, Shanmukha, Kartikeya, Murugan: all the same young commander.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-tarakasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.tarakasura|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.shukracharya-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.shukracharya:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Teacher Who Could Bring Anyone Back","text":"\"शुक्राचार्य असुरों के गुरु थे, और वे किसी भी युग के महानतम विद्वानों में से एक थे। उन्होंने घोर परिश्रम से संजीवनी विद्या भी पा ली थी — वह ज्ञान जो मरे हुए को फिर से जीवित कर देता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Shukracharya was the guru of the asuras, and he was one of the great scholars of any age. He had also, through immense effort, come to know the Sanjivani vidya — the knowledge that brings the dead back to life.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-shukracharya.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.shukracharya|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.shukracharya-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.shukracharya:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Teacher Who Could Bring Anyone Back","text":"\"जिसने इस युद्ध को जीत पाना असंभव बना दिया। देवता गिरते तो गिरे ही रह जाते। असुर गिरते और अगली सुबह फिर उठ खड़े होते। देवता हर एक दिन जीत सकते थे, पर फिर भी एक कदम आगे नहीं बढ़ पाते थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Which made a war unwinnable. Devas fell and stayed fallen. Asuras fell and got up in the morning. The devas could win every single day and be no further forward.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-shukracharya.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.shukracharya|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.shukracharya-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.shukracharya:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Teacher Who Could Bring Anyone Back","text":"तो देवताओं ने एक बड़ा दिलचस्प काम किया। उन्होंने न तो उसे चुराया और न ही उन पर हमला किया। उन्होंने उनके पास एक शिष्य भेजा — अपने ही गुरु के बेटे कच को — ताकि वह उनसे विद्या सीखने की विनती करे।","lang":"hi","body":"So the devas did something interesting. They did not steal it and they did not attack him. They sent him a student — Kacha, the son of their own guru — to ask to be taught.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-shukracharya.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.shukracharya|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.shukracharya-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.shukracharya:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Teacher Who Could Bring Anyone Back","text":"और शुक्राचार्य ने, यह भली-भाँति जानते हुए भी कि उनके दरवाज़े पर किसका बेटा आया है, उसे अपना लिया और उसे सिखाया। क्योंकि वे एक गुरु थे, और एक शिष्य ने उनसे सीखने की विनती की थी। कहानियों में यह बात बिल्कुल साफ़ है कि वे सब जानते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"And Shukracharya, knowing perfectly well whose son had turned up at his door, took him in and taught him. Because he was a teacher, and a student had asked. The stories are quite clear that he knew.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-shukracharya.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.shukracharya|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.shukracharya-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.shukracharya:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Teacher Who Could Bring Anyone Back","text":"असुर समझ गए कि क्या हो रहा है और उन्होंने कच को मार डाला, एक बार नहीं, कई बार। और हर बार शुक्राचार्य उसे वापस ज़िंदा कर लाए — क्योंकि उनकी अपनी बेटी देवयानी ने उनसे ऐसा करने को कहा था, और क्योंकि उन्होंने उसे सिखाने का वचन दिया था।","lang":"hi","body":"The asuras worked out what was happening and killed Kacha, more than once. And more than once Shukracharya brought him back — because his own daughter Devayani asked him to, and because he had said he would teach him.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-shukracharya.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.shukracharya|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.shukracharya-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.shukracharya:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Teacher Who Could Bring Anyone Back","text":"आखिरी बार, उन्होंने कच को जला दिया और उसकी राख शुक्राचार्य के ही पीने के रस में मिला दी। इसलिए जब गुरु ने कच को वापस पुकारा, तो जवाब उनके अपने ही अंदर से आया — और अपने शिष्य को ज़िंदा रखने के लिए, उन्हें उसी समय उसे वह विद्या सिखानी पड़ी, ताकि बाद में वह लड़का उन्हें वापस ज़िंदा कर सके।","lang":"hi","body":"The last time, they burned him and mixed the ashes into Shukracharya’s own drink. So when the guru called Kacha back, the answer came from inside him — and to let his student live, he had to teach him the vidya then and there, and let the boy bring HIM back afterwards.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-shukracharya.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.shukracharya|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.shukracharya-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.shukracharya:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Teacher Who Could Bring Anyone Back","text":"और यही वह पल था जब वह विद्या हमेशा के लिए असुरों के पास से चली गई। चुराई नहीं गई। एक गुरु द्वारा दी गई, और वह भी केवल उसी एक तरीके से जिससे उनका शिष्य ज़िंदा बचकर बाहर निकल सके।","lang":"hi","body":"Which is the moment the knowledge left the asuras for good. Not stolen. Given away, by a teacher, in the only order that would let his student walk out alive.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-shukracharya.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.shukracharya|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.bhasmasura-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.bhasmasura:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Gift He Wanted to Try Out","text":"भस्मासुर ने बहुत भारी तपस्या की — सालों-साल की — और शिवजी ने, जो बड़ी आसानी से मान जाने और आगे सवाल न पूछने के लिए जाने जाते हैं, उसे एक वरदान दे दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"Bhasmasura did an enormous amount of hard work — years of it — and Shiva, who is famously easy to please and famously bad at asking follow-up questions, offered him a boon.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-bhasmasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.bhasmasura|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.bhasmasura-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.bhasmasura:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Gift He Wanted to Try Out","text":"और शिवजी ने 'हाँ' कह दिया। उन्होंने वचन दिया था, और वे अपनी बात से पीछे नहीं हटते। कहानियों में इसे उनकी एक सच्ची कमज़ोरी की तरह ही दिखाया जाता है, इसे छिपाया नहीं जाता — वे दे तो देते हैं, और फिर जो दिया है, उसके साथ उन्हें निबाहना पड़ता है।","lang":"hi","body":"And Shiva said yes. He had said he would, and he does not go back on it. The stories treat this as a real weakness of his and do not tidy it away — he gives, and then has to live with what he has given.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-bhasmasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.bhasmasura|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.bhasmasura-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.bhasmasura:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Gift He Wanted to Try Out","text":"और भस्मासुर के मन में सबसे पहला ख्याल — बिल्कुल पहला — यही आया कि इसे शिवजी पर ही आज़माकर देखा जाए। उसी पर, जिसने अभी-अभी उसे यह वरदान दिया था। तो शिवजी भागे, जो कि ऐसा वाक्य है जो आपको रोज़-रोज़ पढ़ने को नहीं मिलता, और भस्मासुर उनके पीछे पड़ गया।","lang":"hi","body":"And the very first thought Bhasmasura had — the very first — was to try it on Shiva. On the person who had just given it to him. So Shiva ran, which is not a sentence you often get to read, and Bhasmasura came after him.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-bhasmasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.bhasmasura|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.bhasmasura-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.bhasmasura:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Gift He Wanted to Try Out","text":"अब स्थिति यह थी। कोई उसे छू नहीं सकता, कोई उससे लड़ नहीं सकता, और वह रुकने वाला नहीं है। ऐसे व्यक्ति पर बस एक ही चीज़ असर कर सकती है, और वह ताक़त तो बिल्कुल नहीं है।","lang":"hi","body":"Now. Nobody can touch him, nobody can fight him, and he is not going to stop. There is exactly one thing left that works on a man like this, and it is not strength.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-bhasmasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.bhasmasura|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.bhasmasura-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.bhasmasura:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Gift He Wanted to Try Out","text":"मोहिनी नाचीं, और भस्मासुर ने — जो किसी से भी उन्नीस दिखना बर्दाश्त नहीं कर सकता था — उनकी हर एक मुद्रा की हूबहू नकल की। हर ताल पर ताल। हर कदम पर कदम। और मोहिनी ने, नाचते-नाचते, बड़े सहज भाव से, अपना एक हाथ अपने ही सिर पर रख लिया।","lang":"hi","body":"Mohini danced, and Bhasmasura — who could not bear to be less impressive than anybody — copied every movement exactly. Turn for turn. Step for step. And Mohini, mid-dance, quite naturally, placed a hand on top of her own head.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-bhasmasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.bhasmasura|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.bhasmasura-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.bhasmasura:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Gift He Wanted to Try Out","text":"और उसने भी वैसा ही किया। और इस तरह भस्मासुर का अंत हुआ — किसी और वजह से नहीं, बस इसलिए कि वह किसी और को खुद से बेहतर दिखने ही नहीं दे सकता था।","lang":"hi","body":"And so did he. And that was the end of Bhasmasura, undone by nothing whatsoever except being unable to let someone else look better than him.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-bhasmasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.bhasmasura|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.banasura-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.banasura:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Asura Who Guarded His Daughter Too Well","text":"बाणासुर महाबली का बेटा था, और अपने पिता की तरह वह एक राजा था, और अपने दादा प्रह्लाद की तरह वह भी परम भक्त था — शिव जी का भक्त। कहानियाँ कहती हैं कि उसकी हज़ार भुजाएँ थीं, और जब शिव जी नृत्य करते थे, तब वह उनसे ढोल बजाया करता था — और यही बात सबको याद रहती है।","lang":"hi","body":"Banasura was Mahabali’s son, and like his father he was a king, and like his grandfather Prahlada he was devoted — in his case to Shiva. The stories say he had a thousand arms, and that he used them to play the drums while Shiva danced, which is the detail everybody remembers.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-banasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.banasura|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.banasura-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.banasura:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Asura Who Guarded His Daughter Too Well","text":"शिव जी इतने प्रसन्न हुए कि वे खुद आकर बाणासुर के दरवाज़े पर पहरा देने लगे। इसका मतलब था कि बाणासुर के किले में कोई भी कदम नहीं रख सकता था, और बाणासुर — जो ढोल बजाने में तो बहुत अच्छा था पर सुनने में ज़रा कच्चा था — इससे ऊबने लगा, और शिकायत करने लगा कि अब उसके पास लड़ने के लिए कोई बचा ही नहीं है।","lang":"hi","body":"Shiva was so pleased that he came and stood guard at Banasura’s own gate. Which meant Banasura’s fortress could not be entered by anybody at all, and Banasura — who was a very good drummer and a less good listener — began to find this boring, and complained that he had nobody left to fight.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-banasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.banasura|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.banasura-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.banasura:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Asura Who Guarded His Daughter Too Well","text":"उसकी एक बेटी भी थी, उषा। और उसने उसे इन सब चीज़ों के पीछे बंद रखा — वे हज़ार भुजाएँ, वह किला, और दरवाज़े पर खड़े भगवान — क्योंकि उसे उषा के भविष्य के बारे में चेतावनी दी गई थी और उसने तय कर लिया था कि इसका हल सिर्फ दीवारें हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"He also had a daughter, Usha. And he kept her behind all of it — the thousand arms, the fortress, the god at the gate — because he had been warned about her future and had decided the answer was walls.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-banasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.banasura|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.banasura-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.banasura:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Asura Who Guarded His Daughter Too Well","text":"उषा ने एक ऐसे नौजवान का सपना देखा जिससे वह कभी नहीं मिली थी। उसकी सहेली चित्रलेखा, जो किसी का भी चित्र बना सकती थी, तब तक तस्वीरें बनाती रही जब तक कि उषा ने एक पर उँगली नहीं रख दी: अनिरुद्ध, खुद कृष्ण जी के पोते। और चित्रलेखा, जिसमें और भी कई हुनर थे, गई और उन्हें ले आई।","lang":"hi","body":"Usha dreamed of a young man she had never met. Her friend Chitralekha, who could draw anybody, drew portraits until Usha pointed at one: Aniruddha, Krishna’s own grandson. And Chitralekha, who had other talents too, went and fetched him.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-banasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.banasura|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.banasura-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.banasura:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Asura Who Guarded His Daughter Too Well","text":"बाणासुर ने अनिरुद्ध को अपने किले के अंदर पाकर बंदी बना लिया। और इस वजह से कृष्ण उसके दरवाज़े पर आ पहुँचे — और शिव उस दरवाज़े की रक्षा का वचन निभाते हुए वहीं खड़े थे।","lang":"hi","body":"Banasura found Aniruddha inside his fortress and took him prisoner. And that brought Krishna to his gate — and Shiva was standing at that gate, having promised to defend it.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-banasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.banasura|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.banasura-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.banasura:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Asura Who Guarded His Daughter Too Well","text":"तो कहानी सचमुच एक असहज मोड़ पर आ पहुँचती है: एक तरफ कृष्ण, दूसरी तरफ शिव, दोनों अपना वचन निभा रहे हैं, और दोनों में से कोई भी ग़लत नहीं है। यह अच्छाई और बुराई की लड़ाई नहीं है। यह तो दो वचनों का आमना-सामना है।","lang":"hi","body":"So the story arrives somewhere genuinely uncomfortable: Krishna on one side, Shiva on the other, both keeping their word, and neither of them wrong. It is not a good-against-evil fight. It is two promises meeting.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-banasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.banasura|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.banasura-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.banasura:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Asura Who Guarded His Daughter Too Well","text":"यह सब बाणासुर के नाश के बिना ही सुलझ गया। शिव ने अपने भक्त के प्राण माँगे और उन्हें बख़्श दिया गया; बाणासुर के पास उसकी हज़ार भुजाओं में से कुछ बची रह गईं और वह वापस ढोल बजाने लगा; और उषा तथा अनिरुद्ध का विवाह हो गया, आख़िरकार ऐसे मामले अंत में इसी तरह तो सुलझते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"It ended without Banasura being destroyed. Shiva asked for his devotee’s life and it was granted; Banasura kept a few of his thousand arms and went back to drumming; and Usha and Aniruddha were married, which is how these things are settled in the end anyway.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-banasura.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.banasura|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.andhaka-gift-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.andhaka-gift:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Asura Who Asked to Be Remembered","text":"यहाँ एक छोटी-सी बात है जिस पर अक्सर लोगों का ध्यान नहीं जाता, और यह इन कहानियों के असर को किसी भी बड़े युद्ध के मुक़ाबले कहीं बेहतर ढंग से समझाती है।","lang":"hi","body":"Here is a small one that people often miss, and it says more about how these stories work than any of the big battles do.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-andhaka-gift.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.andhaka-gift|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.andhaka-gift-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.andhaka-gift:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Asura Who Asked to Be Remembered","text":"शिव की कहानियों में एक ख़ास बात बार-बार देखने को मिलती है। कोई असुर उनसे लड़ता है—अंधक, गजासुर, जालंधर, या आप कौन-सी कहानी सुन रहे हैं उसके हिसाब से कोई और—और हार जाता है। और फिर, आख़िर में, हारने वाले की एक आख़िरी इच्छा पूरी की जाती है। जान बख़्शी नहीं जाती। पर कुछ दिया ज़रूर जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"There is a pattern in the Shiva stories. An asura fights him — Andhaka, Gajasura, Jalandhara, and others depending on which telling you have — and loses. And then, at the end, the losing one is granted a last request. Not spared. Granted something.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-andhaka-gift.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.andhaka-gift|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.andhaka-gift-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.andhaka-gift:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Asura Who Asked to Be Remembered","text":"और हर बार वह इच्छा लगभग एक जैसी ही होती है। मुझे अपने पास रहने दीजिए। जब लोग आपको याद करें, तो मुझे भी याद रखें। आपकी पूजा में मेरी भी कोई चीज़ शामिल हो।","lang":"hi","body":"And over and over the request is the same sort of thing. Let me be near you. Let people remember me when they remember you. Let something of mine be part of how you are worshipped.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-andhaka-gift.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.andhaka-gift|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.andhaka-gift-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.andhaka-gift:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Asura Who Asked to Be Remembered","text":"और शिव वह वरदान दे देते हैं। हर बार। कुछ कहानियों में तो हारा हुआ असुर उनका ही एक सेवक—एक गण—बन जाता है और हमेशा के लिए अपने ही विजेता के घर के दरवाज़े पर खड़ा रहता है, जो किसी भी कहानी के दिए जा सकने वाले अंत से कहीं ज़्यादा अनोखा और दयालु अंत है।","lang":"hi","body":"And Shiva gives it. Every time. In some tellings the defeated asura becomes one of his own attendants — a gana — and stands at the door of his own conqueror’s house forever, which is a stranger and kinder ending than any story needed to give.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-andhaka-gift.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.andhaka-gift|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ds.andhaka-gift-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ds.andhaka-gift:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Asura Who Asked to Be Remembered","text":"ज़रा इसकी तुलना दुनिया की बाकी कहानियों से कीजिए कि वहाँ हारने वाले के साथ क्या होता है। यहाँ हारने वाले से पूछा जाता है कि वह क्या चाहता है। यह कोई नरमी या ढील नहीं है। यह तो इस बात का एक पूरा नज़रिया है कि असल में दुश्मन होता क्या है।","lang":"hi","body":"Compare that with how most stories in the world end for the one who lost. Here the loser gets asked what he wants. That is not softness. It is a whole opinion about what an enemy is.","art":"art/story/sm/ds-andhaka-gift.jpg","route":"#/story/ds.andhaka-gift|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Devas & Asuras"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cheraman-sails-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cheraman-sails:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sailors Who Found the Islands","text":"केरल के तट के पास, नीले समंदर पर हरे मोतियों की मुट्ठी जैसे बिखरे हुए, लक्षद्वीप के द्वीप फैले हैं — भारत के नक्शे की सबसे छोटी, और सबसे खूबसूरत जगहों में से एक। वहाँ के रहने वाले खुद एक कहानी सुनाते हैं कि कैसे किसी ने पहली बार इन द्वीपों को खोजा था।","lang":"hi","body":"Off the coast of Kerala, scattered over the blue like a handful of green beads, lie the islands of Lakshadweep — the smallest of all the places on India's map, and one of the loveliest. The islanders themselves tell a story about how anyone ever found them at all.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cheraman-sails.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cheraman-sails|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cheraman-sails-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cheraman-sails:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sailors Who Found the Islands","text":"कहते हैं कि बहुत समय पहले, केरल तट के एक महान राजा — चेरामन पेरुमल — एक रात अपने महल से निकले और पश्चिम की ओर समंदर पार चले गए, और फिर कभी वापस नहीं लौटे। और उनकी प्रजा इसे ऐसे ही कैसे छोड़ सकती थी? उनकी खोज के लिए जहाज़ तैयार किए गए।","lang":"hi","body":"Long ago, they say, a great king of the Kerala coast — the Cheraman Perumal — left his palace one night and sailed away west across the sea, and did not come back. And his people could not simply let that be. Ships were fitted out to look for him.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cheraman-sails.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cheraman-sails|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cheraman-sails-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cheraman-sails:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sailors Who Found the Islands","text":"\"हम पश्चिम की ओर समंदर के रास्ते चलेंगे,\" नाविकों ने कहा, \"और हर बंदरगाह पर तब तक पूछेंगे जब तक कोई उन्हें देख न ले।\" उन्होंने पानी, चावल और नारियल लादे, सबको अलविदा कहा, और मछुआरों की नावों को पीछे छोड़ते हुए खुले समंदर में निकल पड़े।","lang":"hi","body":"\"We will follow the sea road west,\" said the sailors, \"and ask at every port until somebody has seen him.\" They loaded water and rice and coconuts, said their goodbyes, and went out past the fishing boats into open water.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cheraman-sails.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cheraman-sails|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cheraman-sails-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cheraman-sails:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sailors Who Found the Islands","text":"मगर समंदर के इरादे कुछ और ही थे। दक्षिण-पश्चिम से एक भयानक तूफ़ान उठा — मॉनसून का वही बड़ा तूफ़ान, जिसके आगे किसी की नहीं चलती — और वह उनके पाल, उनकी पतवार, और रास्ते की सारी समझ उड़ा ले गया, और उन्हें कई दिनों तक नक्शे के सूने हिस्से की तरफ़ धकेलता रहा।","lang":"hi","body":"The sea had other plans. A storm came up from the south-west — the big monsoon kind, the kind you do not argue with — and it took their sails, and their steering, and their idea of where they were, and blew them for days into the empty part of the map.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cheraman-sails.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cheraman-sails|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cheraman-sails-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cheraman-sails:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sailors Who Found the Islands","text":"जब आख़िरकार हवा थमी, तो उनके जहाज़ टूट चुके थे और वे बह रहे थे; पीने का पानी ख़त्म हो चुका था, और किसी भी तरफ़ ज़मीन का नामो-निशान नज़र नहीं आ रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"When the wind finally dropped, they were wrecked and drifting, out of fresh water, with no land in sight in any direction at all.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cheraman-sails.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cheraman-sails|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cheraman-sails-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cheraman-sails:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sailors Who Found the Islands","text":"और भोर के समय, देखने से पहले ही उन्हें आवाज़ सुनाई दी — समंदर के बीचों-बीच चट्टानों से टकराती लहरों के सफ़ेद झाग की एक लंबी लकीर। उस चट्टान के पीछे पानी इतना चमकीला हरा था कि असली ही नहीं लगता था, और उस हरे पानी के पीछे रेत थी, और रेत के पीछे नारियल के पेड़।","lang":"hi","body":"And at dawn they heard it before they saw it — a long white line of surf, breaking on a reef in the middle of the ocean. Behind the reef the water turned a green so bright it did not look real, and behind the green there was sand, and behind the sand there were coconut palms.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cheraman-sails.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cheraman-sails|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cheraman-sails-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cheraman-sails:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sailors Who Found the Islands","text":"\"नारियलों में पानी है,\" पानी चीरते हुए किनारे आते सबसे बुज़ुर्ग नाविक ने कहा, \"और लैगून में मछलियाँ हैं, और यहाँ ऐसी एक भी चीज़ नहीं है जो हमें नुकसान पहुँचाना चाहती हो।\" उन्होंने जहाज़ की मरम्मत की। और जब वे घर लौटे और सबको बताया, तो लोग फिर से वहाँ जाने लगे — इस बार जान-बूझकर।","lang":"hi","body":"\"There is water in the coconuts,\" said the oldest sailor, wading ashore, \"and fish in the lagoon, and not one single thing here that wants to hurt us.\" They mended the ship. And when they got home and told everyone, people began to go back — on purpose, this time.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cheraman-sails.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cheraman-sails|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.cheraman-sails-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.cheraman-sails:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sailors Who Found the Islands","text":"मालाबार तट से परिवार आए और वहीं बस गए। उन्होंने मूँगे की चट्टानों को समझा, द्वीपों के नाम रखे, और भी नारियल के पेड़ लगाए, और द्वीपवासी बन गए — और उन्हीं के बच्चों के बच्चों के बच्चे आज लक्षद्वीप के लोग हैं, जो अब भी मलयालम बोलते हैं, अब भी समंदर को किताब की तरह पढ़ लेते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Families came from the Malabar coast and stayed. They learned the reefs, named the islands, planted more palms, and became the islanders — and their children's children's children are the people of Lakshadweep today, still speaking Malayalam, still reading the sea like a book.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-cheraman-sails.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.cheraman-sails|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ubaidullah-lamp-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ubaidullah-lamp:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dream That Crossed the Sea","text":"लक्षद्वीप के लोग मुसलमान हैं, और बहुत लंबे समय से हैं — हर द्वीप के बीचों-बीच मस्जिद है, पाँच वक़्त की नमाज़ से दिन ढलता और निकलता है, और सुबह की नमाज़ के बाद नावें समंदर में उतरती हैं। द्वीप के लोग एक कहानी सुनाते हैं कि कैसे यह धर्म पहली बार पानी के रास्ते उन तक पहुँचा।","lang":"hi","body":"The people of Lakshadweep are Muslim, and have been for a very long time — the mosque is the middle of every island, the day is shaped by the five prayers, and the boats go out after the morning one. The islanders tell a story about how the faith first came across the water to them.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ubaidullah-lamp.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ubaidullah-lamp|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ubaidullah-lamp-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ubaidullah-lamp:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dream That Crossed the Sea","text":"कहते हैं, बहुत समय पहले अरब में उबैदुल्लाह नाम के एक नेक इंसान रहते थे। एक रात उन्होंने एक ख़्वाब देखा — एक साफ़, शांत और सच्चा ख़्वाब — जिसने उनसे कहा कि समंदर पर जाओ, जहाज़ पर सवार होओ, और पूरब के दूर-दराज़ द्वीपों तक यह दीन लेकर जाओ। वे जागे और वह ख़्वाब बाक़ी ख़्वाबों की तरह ओझल नहीं हुआ।","lang":"hi","body":"Long ago in Arabia, they say, there lived a good man named Ubaidullah. One night he had a dream — a clear, quiet, unmistakable dream — that told him to go to the sea, board a ship, and carry the faith to islands far away in the east. He woke up and the dream did not fade the way dreams do.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ubaidullah-lamp.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ubaidullah-lamp|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ubaidullah-lamp-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ubaidullah-lamp:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dream That Crossed the Sea","text":"\"पूरब तो बहुत बड़ी जगह है,\" उनके दोस्तों ने कहा। \"कौन-से द्वीप? कितनी दूर? तुम्हें खाना कौन खिलाएगा?\" और उबैदुल्लाह ने कहा, \"ख़्वाब में यह नहीं बताया गया था। मैं जाकर ही पता लगाऊँगा।\" और वे बंदरगाह गए और पूरब की तरफ़ जाने वाले पहले ही जहाज़ पर सवार हो गए।","lang":"hi","body":"\"East is a big place,\" his friends said. \"Which islands? How far? Who will feed you?\" And Ubaidullah said, \"The dream did not say. I will find out by going.\" And he went down to the harbour and took the first ship sailing east.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ubaidullah-lamp.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ubaidullah-lamp|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ubaidullah-lamp-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ubaidullah-lamp:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dream That Crossed the Sea","text":"दूर गहरे समंदर में, एक तूफ़ान ने जहाज़ के टुकड़े-टुकड़े कर दिए। उबैदुल्लाह लकड़ी का एक तख़्ता पकड़े पानी में जा गिरे। लहरें उन्हें बहा ले गईं, इधर-उधर उलटती रहीं, और दूर ले जाती रहीं — कितनी देर तक, कोई नहीं कह सकता — जब तक कि उन्होंने उन्हें आधे डूबे हुए और पूरी तरह भटके हुए, एक छोटे से हरे-भरे द्वीप के किनारे पर नहीं पहुँचा दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"Far out at sea, a storm broke the ship to pieces. Ubaidullah went into the water holding a plank, and the waves took him, and turned him over, and carried him — for how long, nobody can say — until they set him down, half-drowned and entirely lost, on the beach of a small green island.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ubaidullah-lamp.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ubaidullah-lamp|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ubaidullah-lamp-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ubaidullah-lamp:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dream That Crossed the Sea","text":"वह अमिनी द्वीप था, उन द्वीपों में से जिन्हें आज हम लक्षद्वीप कहते हैं। भोर के समय द्वीपवासियों को अपनी रेत पर एक अजनबी मिला, जिसके पास कुछ भी नहीं था — न कोई सामान, न सोना, यहाँ तक कि जूते भी नहीं। उन्होंने उन्हें पानी दिया, खाना दिया और छांव दी, क्योंकि यही तो किया जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"It was Amini, in the islands we now call Lakshadweep. The islanders found a stranger on their sand at dawn with nothing at all — no goods, no gold, not even shoes. They gave him water, and food, and shade, because that is what you do.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ubaidullah-lamp.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ubaidullah-lamp|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ubaidullah-lamp-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ubaidullah-lamp:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dream That Crossed the Sea","text":"और वे वहीं बस गए, उनकी बोली सीखी, और इतने प्यार से रहे और एक ईश्वर तथा सीधे रास्ते के बारे में इतनी सादगी से बात की कि लोग उनकी बातें सुनने लगे — पहले कुछ लोग, फिर पूरे-के-पूरे परिवार, और फिर वक़्त के साथ, एक के बाद एक कई द्वीप। किसी के साथ कोई ज़बरदस्ती नहीं की गई। यह एक ऐसी बात है जिसका यह कहानी खास ध्यान रखती है: उनके पास किसी पर ज़बरदस्ती करने के लिए कुछ था ही नहीं। उनके पास बस एक सपना था और अच्छा व्यवहार।","lang":"hi","body":"And he stayed, and learned their words, and lived so gently and spoke so plainly about the One God and the straight path that people began to listen — first a few, then households, then, in time, island after island. Nobody was forced. That is a thing the story is careful about: he had nothing to force anyone with. He had a dream and good manners.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ubaidullah-lamp.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ubaidullah-lamp|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ubaidullah-lamp-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ubaidullah-lamp:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dream That Crossed the Sea","text":"उबैदुल्लाह द्वीप के लोगों के बीच ही बूढ़े हुए। जब उनका देहांत हुआ, तो उन्हें अंद्रोत द्वीप पर दफ़नाया गया, और उनकी मज़ार आज भी वहीं है — एक शांत, सफेदी पुती जगह जहाँ दीया हमेशा जलता रहता है, और सभी द्वीपों से लोग दुआ करने और उन्हें याद करने आते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Ubaidullah grew old among the islanders. When he died, he was buried on the island of Andrott, and his grave is there today — a quiet, whitewashed place where the lamp is kept lit, and people come from all the islands to pray and to remember him.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ubaidullah-lamp.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ubaidullah-lamp|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ubaidullah-lamp-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ubaidullah-lamp:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dream That Crossed the Sea","text":"अंद्रोत के पास से गुज़रने वाले मछुआरे आज भी ठीक-ठीक जानते हैं कि पेड़ों के बीच वह दरगाह कहाँ पर है। यह इन सारे द्वीपों की सबसे पुरानी और सबसे अज़ीज़ जगहों में से एक है — वह जगह जहाँ, जैसा कि द्वीप के लोग बताते हैं, वह सपना आखिरकार अपनी मंज़िल तक पहुँच गया।","lang":"hi","body":"Fishermen passing Andrott still know exactly where the dargah stands among the palms. It is one of the oldest and most loved places in all the islands — the spot where, as the islanders tell it, the dream finally arrived at its address.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ubaidullah-lamp.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ubaidullah-lamp|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.odam-race-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.odam-race:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Race Day on the Lagoon","text":"लक्षद्वीप के सबसे दक्षिणी द्वीप मिनिकॉय पर, हर गाँव के पास दौड़ के लिए एक शानदार नाव होती है — लंबी, पतली और किसी साज़ की तरह चमकाई हुई। यहाँ के लोग पाल वाली नावें, जिन्हें वे 'ओडम' कहते हैं, लगभग किसी से भी बेहतर बनाते हैं, और त्योहारों के दिनों में ये नावें लैगून के पानी पर दौड़ लगाती हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"On Minicoy, the southernmost island of Lakshadweep, every village keeps a great racing boat, long and slim and polished like a musical instrument. The islanders build sailing boats — odam, they call the big ones — better than almost anyone, and on festival days the boats race across the lagoon.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-odam-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.odam-race|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.odam-race-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.odam-race:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Race Day on the Lagoon","text":"दौड़ से कई दिन पहले से, बस नाव ही सब कुछ होती है। उसे तेल लगाकर तब तक रगड़ा जाता है जब तक वह चमक न उठे। शाम को मल्लाह अभ्यास करते हैं, और छोटे-छोटे बच्चे उथले पानी में खड़े होकर अपने पिताओं, चाचाओं और बड़ी बहनों को ताल गिनते हुए देखते हैं — क्योंकि हर कोई अच्छी तरह जानता है कि कौन सी टीम किसकी है।","lang":"hi","body":"For days before a race, the boat is everything. It is oiled and rubbed until it shines. The crew practises in the evenings, and small children stand in the shallows watching their fathers and uncles and big sisters count the stroke — because everyone knows exactly whose crew is whose.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-odam-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.odam-race|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.odam-race-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.odam-race:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Race Day on the Lagoon","text":"\"दौड़ की नाव सिर्फ़ मज़बूत बाज़ुओं का खेल नहीं है,\" बूढ़े माँझी हर साल नए मल्लाहों से कहते हैं। \"इस लैगून में मज़बूत बाज़ुओं की कोई कमी नहीं है। दौड़ की नाव का मतलब है दस लोगों का एक बनकर नाव चलाना। जिस दिन तुम यह सीख जाओगे, हम जीतना शुरू कर देंगे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"A race boat is not about strong arms,\" the old steersman tells the new rowers, every single year. \"The lagoon is full of strong arms. A race boat is about ten people rowing as one person. The day you learn that, we start winning.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-odam-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.odam-race|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.odam-race-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.odam-race:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Race Day on the Lagoon","text":"दौड़ की सुबह सबसे पहले दुआ माँगी जाती है, जैसा कि इस द्वीप पर हर काम से पहले होता है — सभी मल्लाह बाकी लोगों के साथ मस्जिद जाते हैं, और नावें रेत पर इंतज़ार करती हैं, और किसी को इंतज़ार से कोई परेशानी नहीं होती, क्योंकि अच्छी शुरुआत से ही काम अच्छा होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"On the morning of the race there are prayers first, as there are before everything on the islands — the crews go to the mosque with everyone else, and the boats wait on the sand, and nobody minds waiting, because a thing goes better begun properly.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-odam-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.odam-race|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.odam-race-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.odam-race:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Race Day on the Lagoon","text":"इस साल, एक टीम के सामने एक मुश्किल आ गई। उनके सबसे मज़बूत मल्लाह के हाथ में चोट लग गई। उस खाली जगह को भरने के लिए किनारे पर दो लोग मौजूद हैं: एक चौड़े कंधों वाला हट्टा-कट्टा मुसाफ़िर जिसने उनके साथ कभी नाव नहीं चलाई, और एक दुबला-पतला चौदह साल का लड़का जिसने दो साल तक हर शाम इसी टीम के साथ अभ्यास किया है।","lang":"hi","body":"This year, one crew has a problem. Their strongest rower has hurt his hand. There are two people on the beach who could take the empty seat: a big, broad-shouldered visitor who has never rowed with them, and a thin fourteen-year-old who has practised with this crew every evening for two years.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-odam-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.odam-race|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.odam-race-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.odam-race:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Race Day on the Lagoon","text":"नगाड़े की थाप के साथ ताल बँधती है और नावें फेंके हुए भालों की तरह तेज़ी से आगे निकल पड़ती हैं। चारों तरफ़ पानी के छींटे। पूरा द्वीप समुद्र किनारे मौजूद है — दादियाँ, नन्हे बच्चे, और अपनी दुकान बंद करके आया दुकानदार — सब अपने गाँव के लिए ज़ोर-शोर से नारे लगा रहे हैं, और लैगून का पानी इतना साफ़ है कि नीचे तलहटी पर दौड़ती नावों की परछाइयाँ साफ़ दिखाई दे रही हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The drum sets the stroke and the boats go off the line like thrown spears. Spray everywhere. The whole island is on the beach — grandmothers, babies, the shopkeeper who shut his shop — roaring for their village, and the lagoon is so clear you can see the boats' shadows racing along the bottom beneath them.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-odam-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.odam-race|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.odam-race-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.odam-race:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Race Day on the Lagoon","text":"वे आधी नाव की दूरी से जीत जाते हैं, और उस चौदह साल की लड़की को कंधों पर उठाकर किनारे लाया जाता है, जो यह दिखाने की पूरी कोशिश कर रही है जैसे उसके साथ तो ऐसा रोज़ ही होता हो।","lang":"hi","body":"They win by half a boat's length, and the fourteen-year-old is carried up the beach on shoulders, trying very hard to look as if this sort of thing happens to her all the time.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-odam-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.odam-race|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.odam-race-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.odam-race:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · Race Day on the Lagoon","text":"और फिर — यह वह बात है जिसकी बाहर से आने वाले कभी उम्मीद नहीं करते — सब मिलकर एक साथ खाते हैं। जीतने वाली टोली, हारने वाली टोलियाँ, सब के सब। यह मुकाबला सिर्फ़ तब तक मुकाबला रहता है जब तक नावें पानी में हैं और उससे एक मिनट भी ज़्यादा नहीं, क्योंकि कल यही औरतें और मर्द उसी समंदर में मछली पकड़ रहे होंगे, और वहाँ वे सब एक ही टोली हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"And then — this is the part visitors never expect — everybody eats together. Winning crew, losing crews, everyone. The race is a contest for exactly as long as the boats are in the water and not one minute longer, because tomorrow these same men and women will be fishing the same sea, and out there they are all one crew.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-odam-race.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.odam-race|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.minicoy-mahl-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.minicoy-mahl:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island That Speaks Mahl","text":"लक्षद्वीप के ज़्यादातर द्वीपों पर मलयालम बोली जाती है, ठीक केरल के उस तट की तरह जहाँ से लोग आए थे। लेकिन नाव लेकर दक्षिण की ओर बढ़िए, बाकी सभी द्वीपों को पार करते हुए आखिरी द्वीप — मिनिकॉय — तक, और भाषा बदल जाती है। यहाँ के लोग महल बोलते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Most of the islands of Lakshadweep speak Malayalam, like the Kerala coast they came from. But sail south, past all the others, to the last island — Minicoy — and the language changes. Here the people speak Mahl.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-minicoy-mahl.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.minicoy-mahl|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.minicoy-mahl-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.minicoy-mahl:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island That Speaks Mahl","text":"महल वही भाषा है जो ठीक दक्षिण में बसे द्वीपीय देश मालदीव में बोली जाती है — मालदीव के लोग इसे दिवेही कहते हैं। इसका मतलब यह है कि मिनिकॉय का एक बच्चा और मालदीव का एक बच्चा, किसी अंतरराष्ट्रीय सीमा के आर-पार भी, अपने-अपने घरों की रसोई वाली भाषा में आपस में बात कर सकते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Mahl is the same language spoken in the Maldives, the island country just to the south — the Maldivians call it Divehi. Which means a child on Minicoy and a child in the Maldives can talk to each other, across an international border, in the language of their own kitchens.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-minicoy-mahl.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.minicoy-mahl|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.minicoy-mahl-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.minicoy-mahl:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island That Speaks Mahl","text":"\"मिनिकॉय तो नक्शे पर लिखा हमारा नाम है,\" द्वीप का कोई रहने वाला आपको बताएगा। \"हमारे द्वीप का हमारा अपना नाम मलिकु है।\" मलिकु — इसे धीमे से बोलिए, बिल्कुल वैसे जैसे वे बोलते हैं। जो द्वीप अपने लिए अपना नाम संभालकर रखता है, वह द्वीप बखूबी जानता है कि वह असल में कौन है।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Minicoy is our map name,\" an islander will tell you. \"Our own name for our island is Maliku.\" Maliku — say it softly, the way they do. An island that keeps its own name for itself is an island that knows exactly who it is.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-minicoy-mahl.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.minicoy-mahl|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.minicoy-mahl-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.minicoy-mahl:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island That Speaks Mahl","text":"नक्शों पर लकीरें खिंचने से बहुत पहले, मलिकु और मालदीव के बीच का समंदर कोई दीवार नहीं था — वह एक रास्ता था। नावें इधर से उधर आती-जाती थीं। शादियों से दोनों तरफ के परिवार आपस में जुड़ते थे। कहानियाँ, गीत और पकवानों के नुस्खे दोनों तरफ आते-जाते रहे। सरहद तो बाद में आई; भाई-बहन पहले आए।","lang":"hi","body":"Long before the map lines were drawn, the sea between Maliku and the Maldives was not a wall — it was a road. Boats went back and forth. Families married across it. Stories and songs and recipes travelled both ways. The border came later; the cousins came first.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-minicoy-mahl.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.minicoy-mahl|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.minicoy-mahl-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.minicoy-mahl:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island That Speaks Mahl","text":"और महल भाषा में एक और अनोखी बात है। यह अपनी ही लिपि में लिखी जाती है, जिसे ताना कहते हैं — और अरबी की तरह, ताना भी पन्ने पर दाएँ से बाएँ लिखी जाती है।","lang":"hi","body":"And Mahl has one more surprise. It is written in its own script, called Thaana — and Thaana runs from right to left across the page, like Arabic.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-minicoy-mahl.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.minicoy-mahl|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.minicoy-mahl-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.minicoy-mahl:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island That Speaks Mahl","text":"बाकी लक्षद्वीप की तरह ही, मिनिकॉय के स्कूल में बच्चे मलयालम और अंग्रेज़ी में पढ़ते हैं। घर पर बातचीत महल में होती है। नानी-दादी का कोई गीत, कोई कहावत, किसी खास हवा के लिए वह सही लफ़्ज़ जिसका किसी दूसरी भाषा में कोई नाम तक नहीं — ये सब महल में ही ज़िंदा हैं, और बच्चे इन्हें अपने साथ सँभालकर रखते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"At school on Minicoy the children learn in Malayalam and English like the rest of Lakshadweep. At home the talk is Mahl. A grandmother's song, a proverb, the right word for a particular wind that no other language bothers to name — those live in Mahl, and the children carry them.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-minicoy-mahl.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.minicoy-mahl|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.minicoy-mahl-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.minicoy-mahl:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island That Speaks Mahl","text":"\"आप भारतीय हैं या मालदीव वालों जैसे हैं?\" एक बार किसी मुसाफ़िर ने मलिकु के एक बूढ़े नाविक से पूछा। उन्होंने बड़ी शराफ़त से सोचा। \"लाइटहाउस अंग्रेज़ों का बनाया हुआ है, टूना मछली सबकी है, भाषा मेरी माँ की है, और यह द्वीप भारतीय है,\" उन्होंने कहा। \"एक इंसान पूरा बंदरगाह हो सकता है। उसे सिर्फ़ एक नाव बनकर रहने की ज़रूरत नहीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Are you Indian or are you like the Maldivians?\" a visitor once asked an old Maliku sailor. He thought about it politely. \"The lighthouse is British-built, the tuna is everyone's, the language is my mother's, and the island is Indian,\" he said. \"A man can be a whole harbour. He does not have to be one boat.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-minicoy-mahl.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.minicoy-mahl|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.minicoy-mahl-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.minicoy-mahl:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island That Speaks Mahl","text":"मिनिकॉय के दक्षिणी छोर पर बना विशाल लाइटहाउस 1880 के दशक से खड़ा है, और यहाँ के लोग नाविकों के रूप में पूरे अरब सागर में मशहूर हैं — मलिकु के लोगों ने बड़े-बड़े जहाज़ों पर काम करते हुए दुनिया भर के बंदरगाहों का सफ़र किया है, अपनी भाषा को अपने साथ ले गए और पूरी दुनिया को समेटकर अपने घर ले आए।","lang":"hi","body":"The great lighthouse at the southern end of Minicoy has stood since the 1880s, and the islanders are famous across the Arabian Sea as sailors — Maliku men have crewed big ships to ports all over the world, taking their language with them and bringing the world home.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-minicoy-mahl.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.minicoy-mahl|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tuna-star-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tuna-star:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Fish at a Time","text":"लक्षद्वीप के एक द्वीप पर, भोर की पहली किरण फूटने से पहले ही, ट्यूना पकड़ने वाली नाव जाग उठती है। मल्लाह सुबह की नमाज़ पढ़ते हैं, कुछ गरमा-गरम पीते हैं, और पानी की तरफ़ चल पड़ते हैं, जबकि आसमान अभी तय ही कर रहा होता है कि उसे कौन-सा रंग ओढ़ना है।","lang":"hi","body":"Before first light on a Lakshadweep island, the tuna boat is already awake. The crew prays the dawn prayer, drinks something hot, and goes down to the water while the sky is still deciding what colour to be.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tuna-star.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tuna-star|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tuna-star-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tuna-star:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Fish at a Time","text":"पहला पड़ाव: लैगून, चारा पकड़ने के लिए — चमचमाती नन्हीं रूपहली मछलियों से भरा एक झोंका, जिन्हें नाव पर समुद्री पानी की टंकी में ज़िंदा और तैरते हुए रखा जाता है। छोटी मछलियों के बिना बड़ी मछली नहीं मिलेगी। समंदर में हर चीज़ एक-दूसरे से जुड़ी है; मछुआरे यह बात तैरना सीखने से भी पहले सीख जाते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"First stop: the lagoon, to catch bait — a shimmering scoopful of tiny silver fish, kept alive and swimming in a tank of seawater on board. Without the little fish there will be no big fish. Everything at sea is connected to everything else; fishermen learn that before they learn to swim.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tuna-star.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tuna-star|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tuna-star-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tuna-star:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Fish at a Time","text":"रीफ़ से आगे निकलकर, निगरानी करने वाला पानी को पढ़ता है। \"पक्षी!\" — जहाँ समुद्री पक्षी गोता लगा रहे होते हैं, वहीं नीचे ट्यूना शिकार कर रही होती हैं। नाव तेज़ी से आगे बढ़ती है, मल्लाह ज़िंदा चारा फेंकते हैं, और कोई समंदर पर पानी की बौछार करता है ताकि सतह झिलमिलाने और उबलने लगे — और ट्यूना खाने के लिए पागल होकर टूट पड़ती हैं, हर चमकती चीज़ पर झपट्टा मारने लगती हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Out past the reef, the lookout reads the water. \"Birds!\" — where seabirds are diving, tuna are hunting beneath. The boat runs in, the crew flings live bait, and someone sprays the sea with water so it flickers and boils — and the tuna go into a feeding frenzy, striking at everything that glitters.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tuna-star.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tuna-star|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tuna-star-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tuna-star:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Fish at a Time","text":"और अब आता है सबसे मशहूर हिस्सा। हर मछुआरे के पास एक छड़ी, एक छोटी डोरी और एक बिना कांटे वाला हुक होता है। मछली फँसी — एक ज़ोरदार खिंचाव — और एक स्किपजैक ट्यूना कंधे के ऊपर से उड़ती हुई डेक पर आ गिरती है। छड़ी और डोरी, एक बार में बस एक मछली, ठीक उसी तरह जैसे उनके दादाजी किया करते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"And now the famous part. Each fisherman has a pole, a short line, and one barbless hook. Strike — a heave — and a skipjack tuna comes flying over the shoulder onto the deck. Pole and line, one fish at a time, exactly the way their grandfathers did it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tuna-star.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tuna-star|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tuna-star-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tuna-star:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Fish at a Time","text":"एक बार एक मुसाफ़िर ने कप्तान से वही सीधा-सा सवाल पूछा: एक बहुत बड़ा जाल डालकर एक ही बार में मछलियों का पूरा झुंड क्यों नहीं पकड़ लेते?","lang":"hi","body":"A visitor once asked the captain the obvious question: why not use a giant net and take the whole school in one go?","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tuna-star.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tuna-star|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tuna-star-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tuna-star:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Fish at a Time","text":"किनारे लौटकर, पकड़ी गई मछलियों से 'मास' बनता है — ट्यूना को उबाला जाता है, धुएँ में पकाया जाता है और तब तक सुखाया जाता है जब तक वह सख्त और गहरे रंग की न हो जाए और महीनों तक चले। मिनिकॉय की यह सूखी ट्यूना सदियों से इन समंदरों में मशहूर रही है; जहाज़ सिर्फ़ इसे खरीदने के लिए इस द्वीप पर आया करते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"Back on shore, the catch becomes mas — tuna boiled, smoked and dried until it is hard and dark and keeps for months. Minicoy's cured tuna has been famous across these seas for centuries; ships used to call at the island just to buy it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tuna-star.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tuna-star|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tuna-star-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tuna-star:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Fish at a Time","text":"और शाम को, दिशा पहचानने का वही पुराना पाठ, जो किसी खानदानी नुस्खे की तरह पीढ़ी-दर-पीढ़ी चला आ रहा था। दादाजी समुद्र के ऊपर, उत्तर की ओर इशारा करते हैं। \"उसे ढूँढ़ो जो अपनी जगह से नहीं हिलता। बाकी सारे तारे रात भर आसमान में चलते रहते हैं। बस वही एक अपनी जगह टिका रहता है, और वह ठीक उत्तर के ऊपर खड़ा रहता है। कभी रास्ता भटक जाओ, तो अपना तारा ढूँढ़ लो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And in the evening, the old navigation lesson, passed down like a family recipe. The grandfather points north, low over the sea. \"Find the one that does not move. All the other stars walk across the sky all night. That one stands still, and it stands over north. Lose your way, find your star.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tuna-star.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tuna-star|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tuna-star-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tuna-star:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · One Fish at a Time","text":"अब तो नावों में इंजन हैं, जीपीएस है, और वॉटरप्रूफ़ थैलियों में फ़ोन भी हैं। दादाजी यह बात जानते हैं। फिर भी वे तारे की पहचान सिखाते हैं। वे कहते हैं, बैटरियाँ ख़त्म हो जाती हैं। आसमान कभी ख़त्म नहीं होता।","lang":"hi","body":"The boats have engines now, and GPS, and phones in waterproof pouches. The grandfathers know this. They teach the star anyway. Batteries run out, they say. The sky does not.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tuna-star.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tuna-star|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.first-coconut-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.first-coconut:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Nut That Crossed the Ocean","text":"यहाँ सबसे छोटे टापुओं की एक कहानी है — वे जो कभी गहरे समुद्र में मूँगे की चट्टान पर बस सफ़ेद रेत का एक टीला भर थे, जहाँ न कोई पेड़ था, न कोई छाँव, न पीने का मीठा पानी, और न कोई रहने वाला।","lang":"hi","body":"Here is a tale for the smallest islands — the ones that began as nothing but a white sandbank on a coral reef, far out at sea, with no tree, no shade, no fresh water, and nobody home.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-first-coconut.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.first-coconut|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.first-coconut-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.first-coconut:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Nut That Crossed the Ocean","text":"दूर कहीं, किसी हरे-भरे तट पर, नारियल का एक पेड़ पानी की ओर झुका हुआ था, जैसे वे हमेशा झुकते हैं — नारियल के पेड़ हमेशा समुद्र की तरफ़ ही झुकते हैं, मानो किसी बात को सुनने की कोशिश कर रहे हों। और एक दिन एक पका हुआ नारियल डाल से छूटा, नीचे गिरा, गीली रेत पर एक बार उछला, और लहरों में लुढ़क गया।","lang":"hi","body":"Far away, on some green coast, a coconut palm leaned out over the water, the way they do — coconut palms always lean towards the sea, as if they are listening for something. And one day a ripe nut let go, dropped, bounced once on the wet sand, and rolled into the waves.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-first-coconut.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.first-coconut|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.first-coconut-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.first-coconut:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Nut That Crossed the Ocean","text":"\"तुम डूब जाओगे,\" ऊपर से एक समुद्री पक्षी ने नारियल से कहा। \"वहाँ आगे सब कुछ डूब जाता है।\" लेकिन नारियल नहीं डूबा। वह तैरता रहा — पानी की सतह पर शांत और टिका हुआ, जैसे किसी बेहद अकलमंद कारीगर की बनाई एक छोटी सी भूरी नाव।","lang":"hi","body":"\"You will drown,\" a gull told the coconut, from above. \"Everything drowns out there.\" But the coconut did not drown. It floated — riding low and calm, like a small brown boat that had been designed by someone very clever.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-first-coconut.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.first-coconut|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.first-coconut-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.first-coconut:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Nut That Crossed the Ocean","text":"\"हफ़्तों तक वह पानी की लहरों पर बहता रहा। उसके ऊपर से तूफ़ान गुज़र गए। बड़ी-बड़ी मछलियों ने उसे देखा और छोड़ दिया। उसमें वैसा ही धीरज था जैसा सिर्फ़ बीजों में होता है — यानी पूरा का पूरा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"It rode the currents for weeks. Storms passed over it. Big fish looked at it and decided against it. It was patient the way only seeds are patient — which is completely.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-first-coconut.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.first-coconut|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.first-coconut-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.first-coconut:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Nut That Crossed the Ocean","text":"\"और आख़िरकार बाकी सबसे ऊँची एक लहर ने उसे उठाया और समंदर के बीचों-बीच एक सफ़ेद रेतीले टीले पर ऊपर पहुँचा दिया — पानी के घेरे से ऊपर, गुनगुनी रेत में, हज़ार मील के दायरे की उस अकेली जगह पर जहाँ से वह अपनी नई शुरुआत कर सकता था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And at last a wave, taller than the rest, picked it up and set it down high on the white sandbank in the middle of the sea — above the tide line, in the warm sand, in the one place in a thousand miles where it could begin.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-first-coconut.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.first-coconut|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.first-coconut-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.first-coconut:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Nut That Crossed the Ocean","text":"\"उसने अपना ही पानी पिया। उसने अपनी ही ख़ुराक खाई। उसने उस रेत में जड़ें जमाईं जिसमें पहले कभी कोई जड़ नहीं गई थी, और पंख जैसी एक हरी पत्ती ऊपर निकाल दी। टापू का पहला पेड़। समुद्री पक्षी उस पर आकर बैठने लगे, और उनके आने से दूसरी चीज़ों के बीज भी पहुँचे, और धीरे-धीरे वह रेतीला टीला हरा-भरा हो गया।\"","lang":"hi","body":"It drank its own water. It ate its own food. It put down roots into sand that had never held a root before, and sent up one green feather of a leaf. The first tree on the island. The gulls came to sit in it, and their visits brought seeds of other things, and slowly the sandbank turned green.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-first-coconut.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.first-coconut|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.first-coconut-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.first-coconut:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Nut That Crossed the Ocean","text":"\"और जब बहुत समय बाद लोग उस टापू पर आए, तो नारियल के पेड़ उनका इंतज़ार कर रहे थे — फलों में मीठा पानी, छाल से रस्सी, पत्तियों से छतें, तनों से नावें, तेल, छाँव, सब कुछ। लक्षद्वीप के लोग कहते हैं कि इस एक पेड़ की दी हुई चीज़ों के सहारे पूरी ज़िंदगी बड़े आराम से कट सकती है, और यह बात उनसे बेहतर कौन जानेगा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And when, long after, people came to that island, the palms were waiting for them — sweet water in the nuts, rope from the husk, roofs from the leaves, boats from the trunks, oil, shade, everything. The islanders of Lakshadweep say you can live a whole good life in the gifts of this one tree, and they should know.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-first-coconut.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.first-coconut|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.turtle-lagoon-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.turtle-lagoon:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Turtle Who Kept the Lagoon Calm","text":"\"लक्षद्वीप के हर टापू के दो समंदर होते हैं। मूँगे की चट्टानों के बाहर बड़ा गहरा समंदर है, जिसे हमेशा जल्दी मची रहती है और जो हमेशा गरजता रहता है। चट्टानों के अंदर लैगून की शांत झील है — हरे काँच जैसी, नहाने के गुनगुने पानी जैसी, और इतनी थमी हुई कि नाव से नीचे तली पर केकड़े को चलते हुए देखा जा सकता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Every Lakshadweep island has two seas. Outside the reef is the big dark ocean, which is always in a hurry and always shouting. Inside the reef is the lagoon — green glass, warm as bathwater, so still you can watch a crab walk on the bottom from a boat.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-turtle-lagoon.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.turtle-lagoon|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.turtle-lagoon-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.turtle-lagoon:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Turtle Who Kept the Lagoon Calm","text":"लैगून में एक बूढ़ी हरी कछुआ रहती है। वह वहाँ इतने पुराने ज़माने से है जितना किसी की दादी-नानी को भी याद नहीं। वह समुद्री घास के मैदानों को वैसे ही चरती है जैसे कोई गाय खेत में चरती है, और वह ऊपर उठती है, एक धीमी साँस लेती है, और फिर नीचे डूब जाती है — बस यही उसका पूरा दिन है, और उसे इसका कोई पछतावा नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"In the lagoon lives an old green turtle. She has been there longer than anyone's grandmother can remember. She grazes on the seagrass meadows the way a cow grazes a field, and she rises, and takes one slow breath, and sinks, and that is her whole day, and she is not sorry.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-turtle-lagoon.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.turtle-lagoon|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.turtle-lagoon-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.turtle-lagoon:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Turtle Who Kept the Lagoon Calm","text":"टापू के बच्चे आपस में कहते हैं कि लैगून उसी की वजह से शांत रहता है। वे कहते हैं कि हर सुबह, वह मूँगे की चट्टान के अंदर-अंदर धीरे-धीरे एक पूरा चक्कर तैरती है — और जहाँ-जहाँ से वह गुज़रती है, पानी को याद आ जाता है कि शांत कैसे रहा जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"The island children tell each other that the lagoon is calm because of her. Every morning, they say, she swims one slow circle right around the inside of the reef — and everywhere she passes, the water remembers how to be still.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-turtle-lagoon.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.turtle-lagoon|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.turtle-lagoon-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.turtle-lagoon:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Turtle Who Kept the Lagoon Calm","text":"एक मानसून, बाहर का समंदर कई दिनों तक उफनता रहा, और लैगून भी बेचैन होने लगा — नावों को थपेड़े मारता, किनारे की रेत को काटता हुआ। एक छोटा लड़का दौड़कर अपने दादाजी के पास गया। \"कछुआ ने अपना चक्कर लगाना छोड़ दिया है! किसी को जाकर उससे कहना चाहिए कि वह जल्दी करे!\"","lang":"hi","body":"One monsoon, the sea outside went wild for days, and even the lagoon began to fret — slapping at the boats, chewing at the sand. A small boy ran to his grandfather. \"The turtle has stopped swimming her circle! Someone must go and tell her to hurry!\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-turtle-lagoon.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.turtle-lagoon|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.turtle-lagoon-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.turtle-lagoon:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Turtle Who Kept the Lagoon Calm","text":"उन्होंने किनारे से देखा। दूर उस उफनते लैगून में, वह बूढ़ी कछुआ अपना वही चक्कर काट रही थी — वही घेरा, वही रफ़्तार, सूरज के उगने जैसी बेफ़िक्र और शांत, जबकि पानी उसके चारों तरफ़ उछल रहा था और शोर मचा रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"They watched from the beach. Out in the churning lagoon, the old turtle was swimming her circle — the same circle, at the same speed, unhurried as sunrise, while the water leapt and fussed around her.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-turtle-lagoon.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.turtle-lagoon|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.turtle-lagoon-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.turtle-lagoon:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Turtle Who Kept the Lagoon Calm","text":"और जहाँ-जहाँ से वह गुज़र चुकी थी, पानी शांत होता गया। इसलिए नहीं कि उसने उसे दबा दिया था। बल्कि इसलिए, क्योंकि किसी ऐसे के पास रहकर जो बिल्कुल भी घबराने को तैयार न हो, समंदर के लिए भी लगातार घबराते रहना बहुत मुश्किल होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"And wherever she had passed, the water settled. Not because she pushed it down. Because it is very hard, even for a sea, to keep panicking next to somebody who simply is not going to.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-turtle-lagoon.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.turtle-lagoon|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.turtle-lagoon-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.turtle-lagoon:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Turtle Who Kept the Lagoon Calm","text":"शाम तक बाहर का तूफ़ान अब भी गरज रहा था — लेकिन लैगून फिर से शांत लेटा था, नावों को थामे हुए, ताड़ के पेड़ों की परछाइयों को समेटे हुए, बिल्कुल निश्चल और ठहरा हुआ।","lang":"hi","body":"By evening the storm outside was still roaring — but the lagoon lay quiet again, holding the boats, holding the reflections of the palms, holding still.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-turtle-lagoon.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.turtle-lagoon|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.turtle-lagoon-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.turtle-lagoon:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Turtle Who Kept the Lagoon Calm","text":"“उसका सारा हुनर बस यही है,” घर लौटते हुए दादाजी ने कहा। “वह पानी को शांत नहीं करती। वह उसे याद दिलाती है। तुम्हारे अंदर भी ऐसा ही एक कछुआ है — धीमी साँसें, वही गोल चक्कर। जब तुम्हारे अंदर का मौसम शोर मचाने लगे, तो उसे तैरने के लिए भेज दिया करो।”","lang":"hi","body":"\"That is her whole trick,\" the grandfather said, walking home. \"She does not calm the water. She reminds it. There is a turtle like that inside you, too — slow breaths, same circle. When your own weather gets loud, send her swimming.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-turtle-lagoon.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.turtle-lagoon|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.wandering-sandbank-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.wandering-sandbank:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sandbank That Goes Visiting","text":"लक्षद्वीप के द्वीपों में से एक के पास रेत का एक टीला है — लैगून के बीच सफेद रेत की एक छोटी-सी सूनी पहाड़ी, जहाँ न कोई पेड़ है, न झोपड़ी, न कुछ और। किसी-किसी दिन तुम नाव खेकर वहाँ पहुँच सकते हो, उस पर उतर सकते हो, और दुनिया का सबसे छोटा देश सिर्फ तुम्हारा हो सकता है।","lang":"hi","body":"Near one of the islands of Lakshadweep there is a sandbank — a little bare hill of white sand out in the lagoon, with no trees, no huts, no anything. On some days you can row out, land on it, and have the smallest country in the world all to yourself.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-wandering-sandbank.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.wandering-sandbank|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.wandering-sandbank-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.wandering-sandbank:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sandbank That Goes Visiting","text":"और बाकी दिनों में वह बस वहाँ होता ही नहीं। उसी जगह नाव लेकर जाओ तो वहाँ हरा पानी मिलता है, और ठीक उसी जगह मछलियाँ अपने काम में लगी होती हैं जहाँ कल तुम खड़े थे। द्वीप के छोटे बच्चे कहते हैं कि रेत का टीला किसी से मिलने गया है।","lang":"hi","body":"And on other days it is simply not there. Row to the same spot and you find green water, with fish going about their business exactly where you stood yesterday. The little ones on the island say the sandbank has gone visiting.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-wandering-sandbank.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.wandering-sandbank|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.wandering-sandbank-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.wandering-sandbank:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sandbank That Goes Visiting","text":"“किससे मिलने?” कभी न कभी हर बच्चा पूछ ही लेता है। “अपनी माँ से,” दादियाँ कहती हैं, जो पीढ़ियों से यही जवाब देती आ रही हैं। “समुद्र उसकी माँ है। दिन में दो बार तो एक द्वीप भी अपनी माँ के घर जाता है।”","lang":"hi","body":"\"Visiting whom?\" asks every child, sooner or later. \"Its mother,\" say the grandmothers, who have been giving this answer for generations. \"The sea is its mother. Even an island goes home to its mother twice a day.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-wandering-sandbank.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.wandering-sandbank|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.wandering-sandbank-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.wandering-sandbank:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sandbank That Goes Visiting","text":"बड़े बच्चों को इसका असली जवाब पता चलता है, जो उतना ही अच्छा है: ज्वार-भाटा। दिन में दो बार समुद्र साँस अंदर खींचता है और पानी ऊपर चढ़ आता है, और रेत का टीला अपना सिर सिकोड़ते कछुए की तरह नीचे छिप जाता है। दिन में दो बार समुद्र साँस बाहर छोड़ता है, और वह फिर वहीं सामने आ जाता है, सफेद और भीगा हुआ, मानो कुछ हुआ ही न हो।","lang":"hi","body":"The bigger children learn the realer answer, which is just as good: the tide. Twice a day the sea breathes in and the water rises, and the sandbank slips under like a turtle ducking its head. Twice a day the sea breathes out, and there it is again, white and dripping, as if nothing had happened.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-wandering-sandbank.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.wandering-sandbank|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.wandering-sandbank-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.wandering-sandbank:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sandbank That Goes Visiting","text":"और ज्वार को कौन खींचता है? ऊपर देखो। इतनी दूर से चाँद, जब गुज़रता है, तो समंदर को अपनी ओर खींचता है, और समंदर उसकी तरफ़ वैसे ही झुक जाता है जैसे सूरजमुखी सूरज की तरफ़ झुकते हैं। चाँद समंदर को हिलाता है; समंदर रेत के टीले को ढक लेता है। उस रेत पर खड़ा बच्चा मानो चाँदनी से बनी किसी मशीन के अंदर खड़ा हो।","lang":"hi","body":"And who pulls the tide? Look up. The moon, all that way away, tugs at the ocean as it passes, and the ocean leans towards it the way sunflowers lean at the sun. The moon moves the sea; the sea covers the sandbank. A child standing on that sand is standing inside a machine made of moonlight.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-wandering-sandbank.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.wandering-sandbank|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.wandering-sandbank-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.wandering-sandbank:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sandbank That Goes Visiting","text":"एक दोपहर तीन बच्चे नाव खेकर रेत के टीले पर खेलने पहुँचे, और उन्होंने जी भरकर खेला, और खेल अपने सबसे मज़ेदार मोड़ पर ठीक तभी पहुँचा जब पानी की पहली ठंडी उँगली रेत के बीचों-बीच रेंगती हुई आई।","lang":"hi","body":"One afternoon three children rowed out to the sandbank to play, and played hard, and the game reached its absolute best part just as the first cold finger of water crept across the middle of the sand.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-wandering-sandbank.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.wandering-sandbank|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.wandering-sandbank-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.wandering-sandbank:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sandbank That Goes Visiting","text":"वे नाव में बैठ गए और अपने कदमों के निशानों को हरे पानी के नीचे एक-एक करके गायब होते देखने लगे — पहले किनारे वाले निशान, फिर हॉपस्कॉच के खाने, फिर रेत का किला, और फिर वह पूरा का पूरा छोटा सा देश, मानो कहीं सैर पर निकल गया हो।","lang":"hi","body":"They sat in the boat and watched their footprints disappear one by one under the green water — first the ones near the edge, then the hopscotch squares, then the castle, then the whole little country, gone visiting.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-wandering-sandbank.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.wandering-sandbank|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.wandering-sandbank-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.wandering-sandbank:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Sandbank That Goes Visiting","text":"\"यह वापस आ जाएगा,\" सबसे बड़े बच्चे ने कहा, और अगली ही सुबह वह लौट भी आया, धुलकर एकदम साफ़-सुथरा — हर निशान गायब, हर खेल मिटा हुआ, बिल्कुल नई रेत नए-नए खेलों के लिए तैयार। और सच सोचो, तो किसी टापू को चलाने का यह कितना शानदार तरीका है।","lang":"hi","body":"\"It will come back,\" said the eldest, and it did, the very next morning, rinsed perfectly clean — every footprint gone, every game erased, brand new sand ready for brand new games. Which is, if you think about it, a wonderful way to run an island.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-wandering-sandbank.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.wandering-sandbank|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tree-that-counts-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tree-that-counts:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Trees That Count as Family","text":"अंडमान के दक्षिण में, सुमात्रा की ओर एक लड़ी की तरह फैले हुए, निकोबार द्वीप समूह हैं — और वे सबसे पहले और हमेशा निकोबारी लोगों के हैं, जो वहाँ कई सदियों से रहते आए हैं और आज भी रहते हैं। यह कहानी इस बारे में है कि वे किन चीज़ों को अनमोल मानते हैं, और यह उनकी इजाज़त का मान रखते हुए सुनाई गई है: यह उनका हाल बताती है, उनकी जगह खुद बोलने का दावा नहीं करती।","lang":"hi","body":"South of the Andamans, strung towards Sumatra, lie the Nicobar Islands — and they belong, first and always, to the Nicobarese, who have lived there for many centuries and still do. This story is about how they count what matters, and it is told with their leave in mind: it describes, it does not pretend to speak for them.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tree-that-counts.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tree-that-counts|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tree-that-counts-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tree-that-counts:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Trees That Count as Family","text":"बहुत समय पहले निकोबार द्वीप समूह जाने वाले खोजियों ने एक ऐसी बात लिखी, जिसने उन्हें हैरान कर दिया था। जब उन्होंने पूछा, \"यहाँ अमीर कौन है?\", तो किसी ने भी सामान से भरे घर की तरफ़ इशारा नहीं किया। लोगों ने नारियल के बागों, सुअरों और बड़ी-बड़ी डोंगियों की तरफ़ इशारा किया। निकोबारियों के हिसाब से दौलत वह है जो लोगों का पेट भरे और उन्हें यहाँ-वहाँ ले जाए — न कि वह जो किसी बक्से में बंद पड़ी रहे।","lang":"hi","body":"Ethnographers who visited the Nicobars long ago wrote down something that surprised them. When they asked, \"Who is rich here?\", nobody pointed at a house full of things. People pointed at coconut groves, and at pigs, and at big canoes. Wealth, in the Nicobarese way of counting, is what feeds people and carries people — not what sits in a box.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tree-that-counts.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tree-that-counts|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tree-that-counts-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tree-that-counts:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Trees That Count as Family","text":"और यहाँ परिवारों को भी बड़े खुले दिल से गिना जाता है। पारंपरिक निकोबारी परिवार — जिसे 'तुहेत' कहा जाता है — एक बड़ा संयुक्त परिवार होता है: दादा-दादी, चाचा-चाची, बुआ-ताऊ, चचेरे भाई-बहन, सब मिलकर साथ रहते हैं और अपने बाग-बगीचों को साझा रखते हैं। पेड़ किसी एक इंसान के नहीं होते। वे पूरे परिवार के होते हैं, ठीक वैसे ही जैसे परिवार उन पेड़ों का होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"And families are counted generously too. The traditional Nicobarese household — the tuhet, as it is called — is a big joint family: grandparents, uncles, aunts, cousins, everyone together, holding their groves and gardens in common. The trees do not belong to one person. They belong to the family, the way the family belongs to the trees.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tree-that-counts.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tree-that-counts|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tree-that-counts-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tree-that-counts:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Trees That Count as Family","text":"इसलिए जब भी कोई बच्चा पैदा होता है, तो उसके लिए नारियल के पेड़ लगाने की यहाँ बहुत पुरानी परंपरा है। ज़रा सोचिए इसका क्या मतलब है। नारियल के पेड़ पर फल आने में कई साल लगते हैं। जो कोई भी उस नवजात बच्चे के लिए पेड़ लगाता है, वह मानो कह रहा होता है: जब मैं बहुत बूढ़ा हो जाऊँगा, तब भी तुम यहीं रहोगे, हम सब यहीं रहेंगे, और यह द्वीप तब भी हमारा पेट भरता रहेगा।","lang":"hi","body":"So when a baby is born, it has long been the way to plant coconut palms for the child. Think about what that means. A palm takes years to bear. Whoever plants for a newborn is saying: you will still be here, we will still be here, and the island will still be feeding us, long after I am old.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tree-that-counts.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tree-that-counts|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tree-that-counts-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tree-that-counts:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Trees That Count as Family","text":"एक बार किसी मुसाफ़िर ने अचरज में पड़कर पूछा कि जब सिक्कों को गिनना इतना आसान है, तो भला कोई पेड़ों से अपनी दौलत क्यों नापेगा।","lang":"hi","body":"A visitor once wondered aloud why anyone would measure wealth in trees when coins are so much easier to count.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tree-that-counts.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tree-that-counts|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tree-that-counts-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tree-that-counts:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Trees That Count as Family","text":"नारियल के बाग खाना, तेल और पानी देते हैं; सुअर उन दावतों के लिए होते हैं जब पूरा गाँव इकट्ठा होता है; और तराशी हुई, लहरों पर तेज़ी से तैरने वाली नावें इन द्वीपों को आपस में जोड़ती हैं। बगीचों में रतालू और केवड़ा उगते हैं। यह जीने का एक पूरा तौर-तरीक़ा है, जो हमेशा टिके रहने के लिए बना है, और इसे ख़ुद निकोबारियों ने बनाया है।","lang":"hi","body":"The groves give food and oil and drink; the pigs are for feasts, when whole villages gather; the canoes — carved, outrigger-steadied, quick through the surf — knit the islands together. Gardens grow yams and pandanus. It is a whole way of living, built to last, and it was built by the Nicobarese themselves.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tree-that-counts.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tree-that-counts|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.tree-that-counts-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.tree-that-counts:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Trees That Count as Family","text":"द्वीपों पर ज़िंदगी बदली है और बदलती जा रही है — अब वहाँ स्कूल हैं, फ़ेरी नावें हैं और फ़ोन भी हैं, और 2004 की भयानक सुनामी ने इन द्वीपों को बहुत गहरी चोट पहुँचाई थी, फिर भी निकोबारियों ने मिलकर, एक-एक तुहेत के साथ, सब कुछ दोबारा खड़ा कर लिया। उनका वही पुराना हिसाब आज भी ज़िंदा है। सबसे पहले परिवार, और बच्चों के लिए पेड़।","lang":"hi","body":"Life on the islands has changed and keeps changing — there are schools and ferries and phones, and the great tsunami of 2004 hit these islands very hard, and the Nicobarese rebuilt, together, tuhet by tuhet. The counting survived. Family first, and trees for the children.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-tree-that-counts.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.tree-that-counts|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ross-ficus-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ross-ficus:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island the Roots Took Back","text":"अंडमान में पोर्ट ब्लेयर के बिल्कुल पास एक नन्हा-सा द्वीप है, जिसका चक्कर आप एक घंटे में पैदल लगा सकते हैं। सौ-सवा सौ साल पहले, अंग्रेज़ी राज में, यह पूरे द्वीप समूह की छोटी-सी राजधानी हुआ करता था — रॉस आइलैंड, जहाँ हुकूमत चलाने वाले अफ़सर अपने परिवारों के साथ रहते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"Just off Port Blair in the Andamans lies a tiny island you can walk around in an hour. A hundred and some years ago, under British rule, it was the little capital of the whole island chain — Ross Island, where the officers who governed lived with their families.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ross-ficus.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ross-ficus|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ross-ficus-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ross-ficus:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island the Roots Took Back","text":"अपने छोटे-से आकार के बावजूद, यहाँ सब कुछ था: ऊँची मीनार वाला एक चर्च, एक बेकरी, टेनिस कोर्ट, एक छापाखाना, बगीचे, और समंदर की तरफ़ खुलते बरामदों वाले आलीशान घर। लोग इसे \"पूरब का पेरिस\" कहते थे, जो शायद थोड़ी बढ़ा-चढ़ाकर की गई बात थी, लेकिन हज़ार मील के दायरे में यह यक़ीनन सबसे शानदार आधा वर्ग किलोमीटर था।","lang":"hi","body":"For its size, it had everything: a church with a steeple, a bakery, tennis courts, a printing press, gardens, grand houses with verandas looking out at the sea. People called it the Paris of the East, which was laying it on a bit thick, but it was certainly the fanciest square half-kilometre for a thousand miles.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ross-ficus.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ross-ficus|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ross-ficus-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ross-ficus:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island the Roots Took Back","text":"पर यह हमेशा नहीं टिका। 1941 में एक ज़बरदस्त भूकंप ने इस द्वीप को हिलाकर रख दिया, और फिर अंडमान पर दूसरा विश्व युद्ध छा गया, और जब यह सब ख़त्म हुआ तो अंग्रेज़ हमेशा के लिए भारत छोड़कर जा रहे थे। लोग चले गए, दरवाज़े खुले रह गए, और द्वीप पर सन्नाटा छा गया।","lang":"hi","body":"It did not last. A great earthquake shook the island in 1941, and then the Second World War swept through the Andamans, and when it was all over the British were leaving India altogether. The people went away, and the doors stood open, and the island fell silent.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ross-ficus.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ross-ficus|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ross-ficus-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ross-ficus:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island the Roots Took Back","text":"लेकिन कोई द्वीप कभी सचमुच ख़ामोश नहीं होता। कोई चीज़ किनारे पर खड़े होकर शुरू से इंतज़ार कर रही थी — सब्र से भरी, हरी-भरी, और जिसे बिल्कुल कोई जल्दी नहीं थी।","lang":"hi","body":"But an island is never really silent. Something had been waiting at the edges the whole time — patient, green, and in absolutely no hurry.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ross-ficus.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ross-ficus|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ross-ficus-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ross-ficus:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island the Roots Took Back","text":"आज वहाँ जाइए तो आपको कुछ ऐसा दिखेगा जो दुनिया में बहुत कम जगहें दिखा सकती हैं: पेड़ों की बाहों में लिपटी हुई पूरी की पूरी इमारतें। फाइकस की जड़ें दरवाज़ों पर धीमे झरनों की तरह उतरती हैं, खिड़कियों की मेहराबों को लपेट लेती हैं, और चर्च की मीनार पर चढ़ जाती हैं। आप हर बार यह नहीं बता सकते कि दीवार कहाँ ख़त्म होती है और जड़ कहाँ से शुरू — और यही तो कमाल की बात है। द्वीप ने तय कर लिया था कि इन दोनों को एक ही हो जाना चाहिए।","lang":"hi","body":"Go there today and you will see something few places on Earth can show you: whole buildings held in the arms of trees. Ficus roots pour down over doorways like slow waterfalls, wrap window arches, climb the church tower. You cannot always tell where wall ends and root begins — and that is the point. The island decided they should be one thing.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ross-ficus.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ross-ficus|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ross-ficus-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ross-ficus:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island the Roots Took Back","text":"पुराने परेड मैदान में चित्तीदार हिरण चरते हैं। अफ़सरों के बगीचों से मोर कूकते हैं। समंदर की हवा उन कमरों से होकर गुज़रती है जहाँ कभी नाच हुआ करते थे, और अब वहाँ रोशनी के सिवा कोई नहीं नाचता।","lang":"hi","body":"Spotted deer graze on the old parade ground. Peacocks call from the officers' gardens. The sea wind goes through rooms where dances were held, and nobody dances there but the light.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ross-ficus.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ross-ficus|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ross-ficus-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ross-ficus:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island the Roots Took Back","text":"टापू पर एक गाइड इसे कुछ इस तरह समझाता है: \"साम्राज्य ने ईंटों से बनाया और सोचा कि यह हमेशा रहेगा। फ़ाइकस सब्र से बनाता है — और सब्र कहीं ज़्यादा मज़बूत चीज़ है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A guide on the island likes to put it this way: \"The empire built in brick and thought it was building forever. The ficus builds in patience — and patience is the stronger material.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ross-ficus.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ross-ficus|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.ross-ficus-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.ross-ficus:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Island the Roots Took Back","text":"अब इस टापू का एक नया सरकारी नाम है — नेताजी सुभाष चंद्र बोस द्वीप, उस स्वतंत्रता सेनानी के सम्मान में जिनका झंडा इन द्वीपों पर फहराया गया था। फ़ेरी नावें हर रोज़ सैलानियों को लाती हैं, और हिरण उन्हें आते-जाते देखते हैं, ठीक वैसे ही जैसे इस टापू ने हर किसी को आते-जाते देखा है।","lang":"hi","body":"The island has a new official name now — Netaji Subhas Chandra Bose Dweep, honouring the freedom fighter whose flag was raised in these islands. Ferries bring visitors every day, and the deer watch them come and go, the way the island has watched everyone come and go.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-ross-ficus.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.ross-ficus|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.north-bay-light-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.north-bay-light:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lighthouse That Says Its Name","text":"पोर्ट ब्लेयर के पास बंदरगाह के मुहाने पर, नॉर्थ बे नाम की एक हरी-भरी पहाड़ी पर, एक लाइटहाउस खड़ा है — लाल और सफ़ेद पट्टियों वाला, इतने साफ़ पानी के ऊपर कि नीचे के मूँगे के बगीचे पूरे भारत में मशहूर हैं। सालों तक ठीक इसी नज़ारे की तस्वीर बीस रुपये के पुराने नोट पर छपती थी, इसलिए लाखों लोगों ने बिना इसका नाम जाने इस लाइटहाउस को अपनी जेबों में रखा।","lang":"hi","body":"At the mouth of the harbour near Port Blair, on a green headland called North Bay, stands a lighthouse — white and red-banded, above water so clear that the coral gardens below it are famous across India. For years, a picture of this very view was printed on the old twenty-rupee note, so millions of people carried this lighthouse in their pockets without ever knowing its name.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-north-bay-light.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.north-bay-light|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.north-bay-light-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.north-bay-light:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lighthouse That Says Its Name","text":"दिन में तो यह बस यूँ ही खड़ा रहता है और लोग इसकी तस्वीरें लेते रहते हैं। इसका असली काम तब शुरू होता है जब आसमान से रोशनी ढल जाती है और समंदर हज़ारों किलोमीटर में फैली स्याही बन जाता है — क्योंकि उस स्याही पर जहाज़ होते हैं, और ज़मीन को छूने से पहले जहाज़ों को यह जानना ज़रूरी होता है कि ज़मीन कहाँ है।","lang":"hi","body":"By day it just stands there being photographed. Its real work starts when the light goes out of the sky and the sea turns into a thousand kilometres of ink — because out on that ink, there are ships, and the ships need to know where the land is before they touch it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-north-bay-light.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.north-bay-light|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.north-bay-light-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.north-bay-light:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lighthouse That Says Its Name","text":"एक बच्ची, जो लाइटहाउस के रखवाले अपने चाचा से मिलने आई थी, उसने एक बड़ा अच्छा सवाल पूछा। \"लेकिन चाचाजी — किसी नाविक को रोशनी दिखाई देती है। ठीक है। पर उसे कैसे पता चलता है कि वह कौन-सी रोशनी है? दुनिया के हर किनारे पर लाइटहाउस होते हैं। रोशनी तो बस रोशनी होती है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A girl visiting her uncle, a lighthouse keeper, asked the good question. \"But uncle — a sailor sees a light. Fine. How does he know WHICH light? There are lighthouses on every coast in the world. A light is a light.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-north-bay-light.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.north-bay-light|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.north-bay-light-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.north-bay-light:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lighthouse That Says Its Name","text":"\"हर रोशनी रात भर झपक-झपककर अपना नाम बताती है,\" रखवाले ने कहा। \"समुद्री नक्शे में किनारे के हर पैटर्न का हिसाब होता है। नाविक गिनता है — चमक, चमक, ठहराव — और वह ठीक-ठीक जान जाता है कि वह ज़मीन का कौन-सा कोना देख रहा है, और पानी के नीचे चट्टानें कहाँ हैं। रोशनी सिर्फ़ यह नहीं कहती कि यहाँ ज़मीन है। वह कहती है कि यहाँ ज़मीन है, और मैं नॉर्थ बे हूँ।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Every light says its own name, all night, in blinks,\" the keeper said. \"The chart lists every pattern on the coast. A sailor counts — flash, flash, pause — and knows exactly which headland he is looking at, and exactly where the reef lies. The light is not just saying here is land. It is saying here is land, and I am North Bay.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-north-bay-light.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.north-bay-light|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.north-bay-light-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.north-bay-light:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lighthouse That Says Its Name","text":"रखवाले का काम बस लगातार नियम से टिके रहने का है: बत्ती, लेंस और लॉग बुक। इसमें कोई रोमांच नहीं होता, और न ही ऐसा होना चाहिए। दूर अंधेरे में कोई, जिससे वह कभी नहीं मिलेगा, आज रात इसलिए सुरक्षित है क्योंकि रोशनी ने आज भी ठीक वही किया जो उसने कल रात किया था।","lang":"hi","body":"The keeper's work is steadiness itself: the lamp, the lens, the log book. It is not exciting, and it is not supposed to be. Somewhere out in the dark, someone he will never meet is safe because the light did tonight exactly what it did last night.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-north-bay-light.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.north-bay-light|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.north-bay-light-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.north-bay-light:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lighthouse That Says Its Name","text":"यहाँ के समंदर का एक और अजूबा है: पानी खुद कभी-कभी जगमगा उठता है। अंधेरी रातों में, लहरों के हिलने पर पानी के नन्हे जीव चमकने लगते हैं, जिससे नाव के पीछे हल्की आग जैसी लकीर खिंच जाती है। जब से पतवारें बनी हैं, तब से इन द्वीपों के नाविक अपनी पतवारों से रोशनी टपकते देखते आए हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"These waters have another wonder: the sea itself sometimes lights up. On dark nights, tiny living things in the water glow when the waves stir them, so a boat's wake can trail pale fire. Sailors of these islands have watched their own oars drip light for as long as there have been oars.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-north-bay-light.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.north-bay-light|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.north-bay-light-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.north-bay-light:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lighthouse That Says Its Name","text":"और नॉर्थ बे की रोशनी के नीचे, दिन के समय, काँच के तले वाली नावें मूँगे की चट्टानों के ऊपर तैरती हैं — धारीदार मछलियों के झुंड, नीले स्टैगहॉर्न मूँगे, मखमली किनारों वाली विशाल सीपियाँ — एक पूरा शांत शहर, जिसे यह लाइटहाउस पीढ़ियों से जहाज़ों के टूटने से चुपचाप बचाता आ रहा है।","lang":"hi","body":"And under the North Bay light, by day, glass-bottomed boats drift over the coral — clouds of striped fish, blue staghorn, giant clams with velvet lips — a whole silent city that the lighthouse has been quietly guarding from shipwreck for generations.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-north-bay-light.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.north-bay-light|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dugong-meadow-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dugong-meadow:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dugong Who Remembered","text":"ज्यादातर लोग जानते हैं कि समुद्र में मछलियाँ होती हैं। बहुत कम लोग यह जानते हैं कि समुद्र में घास के मैदान भी होते हैं — बिल्कुल असली मैदान, मुलायम हरी समुद्री घास के, जो शांत खाड़ियों के उथले और धूप-खिले पानी में उगते हैं। और जहाँ घास के मैदान होते हैं, वहाँ चरने वाले जीव भी होते हैं। अंडमान और निकोबार द्वीप समूह में चरने वाला यह जीव है डुगोंग: यानी समुद्री गाय।","lang":"hi","body":"Most people know the sea has fish. Fewer know the sea has meadows — real ones, of soft green seagrass, growing in the shallow sunlit water of quiet bays. And where there are meadows, there are grazers. In the Andaman and Nicobar Islands, the grazer is the dugong: the sea cow.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dugong-meadow.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dugong-meadow|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dugong-meadow-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dugong-meadow:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dugong Who Remembered","text":"डुगोंग एक नाव जितनी बड़ी और दादी जैसी सौम्य होती है। उसका गोल चेहरा होता है, छोटी-छोटी दयालु आँखें और मूँछों वाले होंठ, जो घास कुतरने के लिए बने हैं। वह किसी को नुकसान नहीं पहुँचाती। वह अपने मैदान में घास खाती है, साँस लेने के लिए धीरे से ऊपर आती है, एक ठंडी साँस भरती है और फिर घास की ओर नीचे उतर जाती है। बहुत पहले नाविकों ने शाम के धुंधलके में उसे ऊपर आते देखा, और दुनिया की आधी जलपरी कहानियों की शुरुआत हो गई।","lang":"hi","body":"A dugong is big as a boat and gentle as a grandmother. She has a round face, small kind eyes, and a whiskery lip made for cropping grass. She hurts nobody. She eats her meadow, rises softly for a breath of air, sighs, and sinks back to the grass. Sailors long ago, seeing her rise in the dusk, started half the mermaid stories in the world.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dugong-meadow.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dugong-meadow|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dugong-meadow-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dugong-meadow:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dugong Who Remembered","text":"अब सुनिए वह कहानी जो इन द्वीपों का पानी सुना सकता है। एक बूढ़ी डुगोंग उसी मैदान में चरती थी जहाँ उसकी माँ चरा करती थी, और उससे पहले उसकी नानी भी। डुगोंग ऐसी ही होती हैं: वे घास के मैदानों का नक्शा अपनी यादों में सँजोकर रखती हैं, जो पीढ़ी-दर-पीढ़ी चला आ रहा है और इंसानों के किसी भी नक्शे से पुराना है।","lang":"hi","body":"Now for the tale the islands' waters could tell. An old dugong grazed the same meadow her mother had grazed, and her mother's mother before that. Dugongs are like that: they carry the map of the meadows in their memory, handed down, older than anybody's charts.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dugong-meadow.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dugong-meadow|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dugong-meadow-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dugong-meadow:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dugong Who Remembered","text":"एक साल, एक तूफ़ान ने उसके मैदान को उजाड़ दिया — घास को उखाड़ फेंका और रेत के नीचे दबा दिया। उसके पास खड़ी नन्हीं डुगोंग, उसकी बेटी, उस उजड़ी हुई जगह पर गोल-गोल घूमती रही और समझ नहीं पाई कि क्या करे। खाने के लिए कुछ नहीं बचा था, और समुद्र अचानक बहुत बड़ा और बहुत खाली लगने लगा।","lang":"hi","body":"One year, a storm tore her meadow — ripped the grass, buried it in sand. The young dugong beside her, her daughter, circled the ruined place and did not know what to do. There was nothing to eat, and the sea suddenly seemed very large and very empty.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dugong-meadow.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dugong-meadow|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dugong-meadow-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dugong-meadow:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dugong Who Remembered","text":"बूढ़ी डुगोंग ने उसे हौले से छुआ और उस उजड़े मैदान से मुड़कर तट के किनारे-किनारे तैरने लगी। उसे याद आ रहा था: उत्तर की ओर तीन खाड़ियों के पार, जहाँ मैंग्रोव के पेड़ झुके हुए हैं, वहाँ एक और मैदान है। बहुत पहले उसकी अपनी माँ ने उसे वह जगह दिखाई थी, उस दिन की याद जिसकी ज़रूरत उसे आज तक कभी नहीं पड़ी थी।","lang":"hi","body":"The old one nudged her and turned away from the ruin, out along the coast. She was remembering: three bays north, past the point where the mangroves lean out, there is another meadow. Her own mother had shown her, long ago, on a day she had never needed until now.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dugong-meadow.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dugong-meadow|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dugong-meadow-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dugong-meadow:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dugong Who Remembered","text":"वे साथ-साथ तैरीं, बूढ़ी डुगोंग आगे-आगे चल रही थी, उत्तर की ओर तीन खाड़ियों के पार, झुके हुए मैंग्रोव से आगे — और वह रहा मैदान, पानी के नीचे रोशनी में लहराता हुआ हरा-भरा, ठीक उसी जगह जहाँ यादों ने बताया था। उन्होंने अपने सिर नीचे किए और साथ-साथ चरने लगीं, और साथ चलते-चलते बेटी भी वह रास्ता सीख गई।","lang":"hi","body":"They swam together, the old one leading, three bays north, past the leaning mangroves — and there it was, green and waving in the underwater light, exactly where memory said it would be. They put their heads down and grazed, side by side, and the daughter learned the way as she went.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dugong-meadow.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dugong-meadow|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dugong-meadow-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dugong-meadow:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dugong Who Remembered","text":"और उधर उस उजड़े हुए घास के मैदान में, धीमे-धीमे एक नई उम्मीद जाग रही थी: समुद्री घास फिर उग आती है। एक-एक तिनका कर वो पुराना मैदान लौट आया, और एक दिन वो बेटी अपने बच्चे को वापस वहीं ले जाएगी, यादों से बने एक ऐसे रास्ते पर जो कभी मिटता नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"And back at the ruined meadow, something slow and hopeful was happening: seagrass regrows. Blade by blade the old meadow returned, and one day the daughter would lead her own calf back to it, along a path made entirely of remembering.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dugong-meadow.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dugong-meadow|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.dugong-meadow-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.dugong-meadow:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Dugong Who Remembered","text":"डूगोंग अंडमान और निकोबार द्वीप समूह का राजकीय पशु है, और उसे ख़ास सुरक्षा दी गई है — क्योंकि अब बहुत कम डूगोंग बचे हैं, और जो जीव किसी को नुकसान नहीं पहुँचाता, वो ऐसे समंदर का हकदार है जहाँ उसे भी कोई नुकसान न पहुँचे। उसकी रक्षा करने का मतलब है उन घास के मैदानों की भी रक्षा करना। भला कोई घास चरने वाले को बचाकर उसकी घास पर पक्की सड़क कैसे बना सकता है।","lang":"hi","body":"The dugong is the official animal of the Andaman and Nicobar Islands, and it is protected — because there are not many left, and a creature that harms nobody deserves waters that harm her back just as little. Protecting her means protecting the meadows too. You cannot save a grazer and pave her grass.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-dugong-meadow.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.dugong-meadow|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.flying-fox-ferry-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.flying-fox-ferry:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Evening Ferry of the Flying Foxes","text":"अंडमान के द्वीपों पर दिन का अंत एक अनोखे तमाशे के साथ होता है, और यह तमाशा बिल्कुल मुफ़्त है। जैसे ही आसमान सुनहरा होता है, ऊँचे पेड़ों में से पंख फड़फड़ाती एक लंबी, धीमी कतार ऊपर उठती है और पानी के पार निकल पड़ती है — सैकड़ों बड़े और काले साए, किसी फ़ेरी की कतार जैसे बेफ़िक्र और इत्मीनान से चलते हुए।","lang":"hi","body":"On the islands of the Andamans, the day ends with a show, and the show is free. Just as the sky goes gold, a long, slow, flapping line rises out of the tall trees and sets off across the water — hundreds of big dark shapes, unhurried as a ferry queue.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-flying-fox-ferry.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.flying-fox-ferry|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.flying-fox-ferry-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.flying-fox-ferry:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Evening Ferry of the Flying Foxes","text":"ये फ़्लाइंग फ़ॉक्स हैं — इन द्वीपों के विशाल चमगादड़, लोमड़ी जैसे लाल चेहरों वाले, बंद छतरी जैसे मुड़े पंखों वाले, और जिनके फैले पंख तुम्हारी दोनों बाँहों के फैलाव से भी बड़े होते हैं। दिन भर वे अपने बसेरे वाले पेड़ों पर उलटे लटके रहते हैं, पंखों से हवा झलते हैं, आपस में हल्की-फुल्की नोंक-झोंक करते हैं, और बिल्कुल कोई काम नहीं करते। शाम होते ही उनका काम शुरू होता है।","lang":"hi","body":"They are flying foxes — the great fruit bats of the islands, with fox-red faces, wrapped-umbrella wings, and a wingspan wider than your armspan. All day they hang upside down in their roost trees, fanning themselves, bickering gently, doing absolutely nothing. Evening is when their work begins.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-flying-fox-ferry.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.flying-fox-ferry|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.flying-fox-ferry-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.flying-fox-ferry:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Evening Ferry of the Flying Foxes","text":"और यह सचमुच का काम है। बस इन द्वीपों को इस बात का अहसास नहीं है। ये फ़्लाइंग फ़ॉक्स फलों के पेड़ों की ओर उड़ जाते हैं — जंगली अंजीर, जंगली बादाम, जंगलों में उगे आम — और रात भर दावत उड़ाते हैं। वे खाते हुए खूब बिखेरते हैं, और यह बिखेरना ही तो सारा खेल है।","lang":"hi","body":"And it IS work. The islands just do not know it. The flying foxes cross to the fruit trees — wild figs, sea almonds, mangoes gone wild — and they feast all night, and they are messy eaters, and the mess is the whole point.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-flying-fox-ferry.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.flying-fox-ferry|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.flying-fox-ferry-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.flying-fox-ferry:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Evening Ferry of the Flying Foxes","text":"अपनी चाची के साथ शाम को इस पार से उस पार जाते चमगादड़ों को देखते हुए एक लड़के ने उनसे बड़ा अच्छा सवाल पूछा, \"चाची, पानी के उस पार उस छोटे से टापू पर जो जंगल है—उसे किसने लगाया? वहाँ तो कोई नहीं रहता। कभी कोई रहा भी नहीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A boy watching the evening crossing with his aunt asked her the good question. \"Auntie, the forest on that little island across the water — who planted it? Nobody lives there. Nobody ever has.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-flying-fox-ferry.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.flying-fox-ferry|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.flying-fox-ferry-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.flying-fox-ferry:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Evening Ferry of the Flying Foxes","text":"\"इस आने-जाने को देखो,\" चाची ने कहा। \"जो भी चमगादड़ अंजीर खाती है, वह उसके बीज अपने पेट में लेकर उड़ती है, और आज रात इन टापुओं पर कहीं न कहीं वे बीज गिरेंगे—खुली जगहों में, समुद्री तटों पर, और पानी की ऐसी संकरी खाड़ियों के पार जिन्हें तैरकर कोई बीज कभी पार नहीं कर सकता था। ये चमगादड़ इन टापुओं पर तब से जंगल लगा रहे हैं, जब उन्हें ऐसा करते देखने के लिए यहाँ कोई इंसान भी नहीं था।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Watch the ferry,\" said his aunt. \"Every fox that eats a fig carries its seeds away inside her, and somewhere out over the islands tonight, seeds will fall — into clearings, onto beaches, across channels no seed could swim. The bats have been planting these islands since before there was anyone here to watch them do it.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-flying-fox-ferry.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.flying-fox-ferry|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.flying-fox-ferry-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.flying-fox-ferry:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Evening Ferry of the Flying Foxes","text":"दिन के समय ये चमगादड़ जिन पुराने पेड़ों पर लटकते हैं, वे उनके जाने-पहचाने ठिकाने हैं—साल-दर-साल वही पेड़, उन्हीं डालियों पर चमगादड़ों की पीढ़ियाँ, मानो कोई ऐसा परिवार जिसने कभी अपना घर ही न बदला हो। टापू के लोग इन्हीं के सहारे रास्ते तय करते हैं: 'चमगादड़ वाले पेड़ों से मुड़ जाना', और हर किसी को पता होता है कि वह जगह कहाँ है।","lang":"hi","body":"The old trees the foxes hang in by day are known roosts — the same trees, year after year, generations of bats in the same branches, like a family that has never once moved house. Islanders navigate by them: turn at the bat trees, everyone knows where that is.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-flying-fox-ferry.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.flying-fox-ferry|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.flying-fox-ferry-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.flying-fox-ferry:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Evening Ferry of the Flying Foxes","text":"लड़का और उसकी चाची तब तक देखते रहे जब तक कि पीछे छूटे आखिरी चमगादड़ भी पार नहीं निकल गए—शाम के गुलाबी आसमान में छोटे-छोटे काले कॉमा जैसे। \"वे भोर होने से पहले लौट आएँगे,\" चाची ने कहा। \"फलों से पेट भरे हुए, और घर लौटने के पूरे रास्ते में पेड़ लगाते हुए। सोना, स्कूल, खाना—यह तुम्हारा नियम है। लटकना, उड़ना, और जंगल उगाना—यह उनका नियम है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The boy and his aunt watched until the last stragglers crossed, little black commas against the pink. \"They will be back before dawn,\" she said. \"Full of fruit, planting all the way home. Sleep, school, dinner — that is your schedule. Hang, fly, plant a forest — that is theirs.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-flying-fox-ferry.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.flying-fox-ferry|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.one-island-bird-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.one-island-bird:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird With One Island","text":"मुख्य अंडमान द्वीपों से बहुत दूर, खुले समंदर में अकेला, नारकोंडम नाम का एक छोटा, हरा-भरा ज्वालामुखीय टापू है। वहाँ ऊँची चट्टानें हैं, जंगल हैं, कोई शहर नहीं, और एक ऐसा निवासी है जिसने पक्षी-प्रेमियों के बीच इस जगह को मशहूर बना दिया है: नारकोंडम हॉर्नबिल।","lang":"hi","body":"Far out beyond the main Andaman Islands, alone in the open sea, stands a small green volcanic island called Narcondam. It has cliffs, forest, no town, and one resident that has made it famous among people who love birds: the Narcondam hornbill.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-one-island-bird.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.one-island-bird|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.one-island-bird-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.one-island-bird:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird With One Island","text":"\"हॉर्नबिल सचमुच एक अनोखा परिंदा होता है — एक बड़ा, खूबसूरत पक्षी जिसकी भारी-भरकम मुड़ी हुई चोंच होती है, और जो अंजीर की तलाश में पेड़ों की डालियों के बीच गोते लगाता रहता है। भारत के कई जंगलों में हॉर्नबिल मिलते हैं। लेकिन यह वाला हॉर्नबिल सिर्फ़ नारकोंडम द्वीप पर ही रहता है। न पास वाले द्वीप पर। न मुख्य ज़मीन पर। पूरी दुनिया में कहीं और नहीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A hornbill is a spectacular thing — a big handsome bird with a huge curved bill, swooping through the canopy after figs. There are hornbills in many forests of India. But THIS hornbill lives on Narcondam Island only. Not the next island. Not the mainland. Nowhere else on the entire planet.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-one-island-bird.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.one-island-bird|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.one-island-bird-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.one-island-bird:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird With One Island","text":"\"वैज्ञानिकों के पास इसके लिए एक शब्द है: एंडेमिक। इसका मतलब है \"सिर्फ़ यहीं मिलने वाला।\" दुनिया भर के सारे नारकोंडम हॉर्नबिल — जितने भी मौजूद हैं, सब के सब — बस एक ऐसे छोटे से द्वीप पर समा जाते हैं जिसे आप एक ही दोपहर में पैदल चलकर पार कर सकते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Scientists have a word for that: endemic. It means \"found only here.\" The whole world population of Narcondam hornbills — every single one that exists — fits on one island you could walk across in an afternoon.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-one-island-bird.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.one-island-bird|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.one-island-bird-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.one-island-bird:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird With One Island","text":"\"हॉर्नबिल जिस तरह अपना परिवार पालते हैं, वह किसी मनगढ़ंत कहानी जैसा लगता है, पर है बिल्कुल सच। माँ पक्षी किसी बड़े, पुराने पेड़ में एक खोखली जगह ढूंढती है, अंदर जाकर बैठ जाती है, और कीचड़ व लेप से अंदर से ही दरवाज़ा बंद कर लेती है — बस एक पतली सी झिरी छोड़कर। वह अपने अंडों के साथ उस चारदीवारी में बंद रहती है, हर सांप और तूफ़ान से पूरी तरह सुरक्षित।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Hornbills raise their families in a way that sounds made up and is not. The mother finds a hollow in a big old tree, settles in, and seals the entrance from inside with mud and paste — leaving only a narrow slit. She stays walled in with her eggs, safe from every snake and storm.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-one-island-bird.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.one-island-bird|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.one-island-bird-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.one-island-bird:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird With One Island","text":"\"पर इससे एक साफ़ मुश्किल खड़ी होती है: दीवार के अंदर बंद माँ ख़रीदारी करने बाहर नहीं जा सकती।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Which leaves one obvious problem: a walled-in mother cannot go shopping.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-one-island-bird.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.one-island-bird|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.one-island-bird-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.one-island-bird:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird With One Island","text":"\"और यही तो एक खूबसूरत चक्र है: हॉर्नबिल जंगल के अंजीर खाकर जीते हैं, और जंगल हॉर्नबिलों के दम पर जीता है — जो बीज वे निगलकर इधर-उधर बिखेरते हैं, उन्हीं से अंजीर के नए पेड़ उगते हैं। एक द्वीप, एक पक्षी, एक जंगल, जो हज़ारों सालों से इसी तरह एक-दूसरे का साथ निभाते चले आ रहे हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"And here is the beautiful circle: the hornbills live on the forest's figs, and the forest lives on the hornbills — the seeds they swallow and scatter grow into the next generation of fig trees. One island, one bird, one forest, each keeping the other going, round and round, for thousands of years.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-one-island-bird.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.one-island-bird|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.one-island-bird-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.one-island-bird:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird With One Island","text":"\"जिस जीव के पास बस एक ही द्वीप हो, उसके पास कोई दूसरा सहारा नहीं होता। अगर नारकोंडम पर कुछ बहुत बुरा हो जाए — जैसे पेड़ कट जाएं, या बाहर से नए जानवर आ जाएं — तो इनकी गिनती आगे बढ़ाने के लिए दुनिया में कहीं और कोई दूसरा झुंड नहीं बचेगा। इसलिए इस द्वीप को एक अभयारण्य बनाकर सुरक्षित रखा गया है, यहाँ आने-जाने पर कड़ी रोक है, और वैज्ञानिक हॉर्नबिलों की गिनती बड़े ध्यान से करते हैं। हाल के सालों की गिनती एक अच्छी ख़बर लेकर आई है: एक द्वीप वाला यह पक्षी अब भी हिम्मत से टिका हुआ है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"A creature with one island has no spare. If anything went badly wrong on Narcondam — the trees cut, new animals brought ashore — there would be no second population out there to carry on. So the island is protected as a sanctuary, visits are strictly limited, and scientists count the hornbills carefully. The counts in recent years have been good news: the bird with one island is holding on.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-one-island-bird.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.one-island-bird|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.one-island-bird-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.one-island-bird:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bird With One Island","text":"\"भारत में ऐसी अनमोल धरोहरें बिखरी पड़ी हैं — ऐसे जीव-जंतु जिनकी पूरी दुनिया बस एक पहाड़ी, एक झील या एक टापू तक ही सिमटी है। ये हमारे देश की सबसे नायाब चीज़ें हैं, किसी भी तिजोरी में रखे ख़ज़ाने से कहीं ज़्यादा कीमती, क्योंकि तिजोरी का ख़ज़ाना तो दोबारा भी आ सकता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"India is dotted with treasures like this — species whose entire world is one hill, one lake, one island. They are the country's rarest belongings, rarer than anything in any vault, because a vault's treasures can be replaced.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-one-island-bird.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.one-island-bird|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.island-of-tongues-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.island-of-tongues:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bazaar of Many Tongues","text":"\"पोर्ट ब्लेयर के सुबह के बाज़ार में जाओ — अंडमान का मुख्य शहर, जिसे हाल ही में 'श्री विजय पुरम' का नया सरकारी नाम दिया गया है — और बस ध्यान से सुनो। मछली की दुकान पर बांग्ला। फूलों की दुकान पर तमिल। तेलुगु, मलयालम, हिंदी, दक्षिणी द्वीपों से आई निकोबारी, और सैलानियों के नक्शों पर बोली जाती अंग्रेज़ी। एक छोटा सा बाज़ार, और लगता है जैसे आधा भारत एक साथ बोल रहा हो।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Go to the morning market in Port Blair — the main town of the Andamans, lately given the new official name Sri Vijaya Puram — and just listen. Bengali at the fish stall. Tamil at the flower stall. Telugu, Malayalam, Hindi, Nicobarese from the southern islands, English over the tourist maps. One small market, half of India talking at once.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-island-of-tongues.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.island-of-tongues|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.island-of-tongues-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.island-of-tongues:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Bazaar of Many Tongues","text":"\"हर भाषा अपने साथ एक कहानी लेकर यहाँ पहुँची। पिछली डेढ़ सदी में बंगाल और तमिल इलाके से, केरल, आंध्र और राँची के पठार से लोग इन द्वीपों पर आकर बसे — किसान, मज़दूर, मछुआरे, क्लर्क — और हर परिवार ने अपने चूल्हे-बर्तनों के साथ-साथ अपनी भाषा भी बाँध ली थी। ये द्वीप मानो एक छोटा सा भारत बन गए, समंदर के नमकीन स्वाद में रंगा हुआ।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Every language arrived with a story. Over the last century and a half, settlers came to these islands from Bengal and from Tamil country, from Kerala and Andhra and the Ranchi plateau — farmers, labourers, fisherfolk, clerks — and each family packed its language along with its cooking pots. The islands became a little India, sea-flavoured.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-island-of-tongues.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.island-of-tongues|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","East & the Islands"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]}});
